    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DATE: Sunday July 26th, 2015  STAGE: NOTL Public Library  ADDRESS: 10 Anderson Ln, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON L0S 1J0  TIME: 2:00pm - 3:30pm  TICKET PRICE: $10 + HST    &quot;(De) Constructing the Archtop Jazz Guitar Workshop with Paul Saunders&quot;  Followed by a jazz guitar demo with jazz guitarist Warren Stirtzinger.    A close look at the way the archtop jazz guitar is made; construction techniques, methods and materials. including a concise look at the evolution of the instrument and its place in jazz music now and in the future from the perspective of a guitar maker.    An archtop guitar is a steel-stringed acoustic or semi-acoustic guitar with a full body and a distinctive arched top, whose sound is particularly popular with jazz players.    Typically, an archtop guitar has:      6 strings    An arched top and back, not flat    Moveable adjustable bridge    F-holes similar to members of the violin family    Rear mounted tailpiece, stoptail bridge or Bigsby tremolo    14th-fret neck join    WEBSITE: www.paulsaundersinstruments.com"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "(De)Constructing the Archtop Jazz Guitar Workshop with Paul Saunders"
      }
    ],
