    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "    Twilight Jazz Series - St. Catharines Edition  Featuring: Jack de Keyzer    Two time Juno winner, blues guitarist, singer, song writer Jack de Keyzer plays the blues world wide. His music has taken him from the Arctic Circle to Puerto Escondido, Mexico; from Athens, Greece to Hornby Island, BC &amp; many points in between.    One of Canada’s most awarded and in demand blues guitarists, Jack has released 10 CD’s and 1 DVD. An exciting live performer, soulful vocalist &amp; world class song writer, de Keyzer performs an average of 150 shows per year &amp; has brought audiences to their feet at many major Jazz &amp; Blues Festivals including the Montreal Jazz Fest, Blues Sur Seine (France) The Ottawa Blues Festival &amp; Puerto Blues, (Mexico).    Much celebrated, de Keyzer has been nominated for the Juno (Blues Album) 5 X and won the Juno twice in 2003 &amp; 2010. He has also won 7 Maple Blues Awards, (Canada’s national blues awards) 1st place in the Intl Songwriting Competition &amp; CBC’s Great Canadian Blues Award from a poll of radio listeners.    Jack de Keyzer will have you rocking in your seat to his hot blues, R&amp;B &amp; cool soul jazz. World class.    “If Jack de Keyzer was from Chicago, New York or LA, he’d be famous” Bob Dylan “The finest blues guitarist in Canada” Jeff Healey.    Go to www.twilightjazz.ca for more info."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Twilight Jazz Series - January Blues"
      }
    ],
