    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  Featuring: Jack de Keyzer      EVENT: Twilight Jazz Series: St. Catharines edition –January Blues  DATE: Sunday,  January 5, 2020  TIME: 6 PM – 9 PM  LOCATION: Mahtay Cafe and Lounge  ADDRESS: 241 St. Paul St., St. Catharines, ON  TICKET PRICE: $15 + HST in advance / $20 + HST at the door / $10+ HST for Musicians and Arts Workers / $8 + HST for students    Buy Tickets    SEASON'S PASSES are also available:  ONLY $99 for all 8 shows from November to June:    Buy Passes    ABOUT THE SHOW:  Info coming soon...    BIO:    Two time Juno winner, blues guitarist, singer, songwriter Jack de Keyzer plays the blues worldwide. His music has taken him from the Arctic Circle to Puerto Escondido, Mexico; from Athens, Greece to Hornby Island, BC &amp; many points in between.    One of Canada’s most awarded and in-demand blues guitarists, Jack has released 10 CD’s and 1 DVD. An exciting live performer, soulful vocalist &amp; world-class songwriter, de Keyzer performs an average of 150 shows per year &amp; has brought audiences to their feet at many major Jazz &amp; Blues Festivals including the Montreal Jazz Fest, Blues Sur Seine (France) The Ottawa Blues Festival &amp; Puerto Blues, (Mexico).    Much celebrated, de Keyzer has been nominated for the Juno (Blues Album) 5 X and won the Juno twice in 2003 &amp; 2010. He has also won 7 Maple Blues Awards, (Canada’s national blues awards) 1st place in the Intl Songwriting Competition &amp; CBC’s Great Canadian Blues Award from a poll of radio listeners.    Jack de Keyzer will have you rocking in your seat to his hot blues, R&amp;B &amp; cool soul jazz. World-class.    “If Jack de Keyzer was from Chicago, New York or LA, he’d be famous” Bob Dylan “The finest blues guitarist in Canada” Jeff Healey.    &nbsp;"
      }
    ],
