    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DATE:            Tuesday, May 26, 2020  TIME:              6:00 pm – 7:00 pm EST  VENUE:          Shady Acres Studio (St. Catharines) and Burnaby, BC (This event will be Live streamed)  PRICE:            FREE (Donations accepted)             Mask made from                        Austin Patterson  broken jewellery    To donate and help support the festival:      * Please note that donations accepted help the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) continue to bring live music and events to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!    [embed]https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lmu4MVteFRY[/embed]  CLICK HERE for info about AUSTIN              WORKSHOP DESCRIPTION:    In this mask making tutorial, you will learn how to create a fabulous and inexpensive masquerade/ Mardi Gras mask out of basic art supplies.      [caption id=&quot;attachment_16734&quot; align=&quot;aligncenter&quot; width=&quot;500&quot;] Materials: Mask, Small wooden dowel or chopsticks, Hot glue gun and glue sticks. Options for decorating: Recycled fabrics, Glitter, Paint, Feathers, Fake flowers, Recycled jewellery.[/caption]              &nbsp;  Places to find materials:  Walmart  Michaels  Dollar store  &nbsp;"
      }
    ],
