    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/livestream-love-jazz-series-27-featuring-greg-rodman/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DATE:            Friday June 19, 2020  TIME:             7:00 pm – 8:00 pm EDST  VENUE:         'In Your Own Backyard' (This event will be Live streamed)  PRICE:           FREE (Donations accepted)    * Please note that donations accepted to help the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!  [embed]https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6R6M8RzJaCk[/embed]  To tip the band:    To donate and help support the festival:          ABOUT GREG RODMAN:      Greg Rodman’s musical life has been an eclectic one. Equally at home on both acoustic and electric guitars, his style and concept are unique, and are characterized by an unusual depth of emotion, backed by dazzling technique. After studying at Boston’s Berklee College on a scholarship, Greg honed his craft playing in studios, showbands, and jazz groups.To date, Greg has performed in more than 120 countries, and has played for numerous stars and dignitaries including Anna Maria Alberghetti, Rita Moreno, The Fifth Dimension, Charo, Regis Philbin, Carol Pope, John Davidson, Bobby Rydel, Roger Williams, Florence Henderson, Shirley Jones, Sergio Franchi, Joel Gray, Jim Nabors, Pat Boone, Hal Linden, Frank Gorshen, and Jim Stafford.    Greg has two main concert shows. “Guitar on the Edge” features original and unique arrangements of music from various cultures and places around the world.”Spanish Guitar Fire” focuses on romantic and virtuoso pieces from Spain, South America and the Caribbean.    Artist Website  www.gregrodman.com/            ABOUT THE “LIVEStream.LOVE.JAZZ.Series&quot;    “We love organically grown events and this series is a prime example of that. In January of 2019, we started a series called &quot;IN YOUR OWN BACKYARD&quot; when local jazz pianist Doug Mundy asked us if we could store his Steinway grand piano at our Shady Acres Studio. We knew how our jazz fans LOVE the intimate concerts so we thought why not do one ‘In our own back yard’.    The first 4-part piano series was a huge success so we then decided to add another 4 shows and then another 2! 10 shows in total for 2019 and when the piano was removed we decided to continue with a guitar series. Part 4 of the guitar series came during the COVID-19 pandemic so we decided to adapt to the times. Our NEW live-streamed events are now in YOUR own backyard.  ‘From our back yard to yours’    To align with our tag line:  LIVE LOVE JAZZ and the current situation, we have re-branded our series to be called the “LIVEStream.LOVE.JAZZ.Series&quot;.    We do look forward to having our guests gather in our backyard again soon (when it is safe to do so) but until then we are thrilled to be able to live-stream our events and to keep the music alive in Niagara and beyond”    Juliet Dunn and Peter Shea (Co-creators: Twilight Jazz Series and TD Niagara Jazz Festival)    Find us online : www.NiagaraJazzFestival.com  Call us at: 1-844-LIV-JAZZ (1-844-548-5299)  Thank you to our generous sponsors for their donations:  [rev_slider alias=&quot;llj-sponsors&quot;]"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "LIVEstream.LOVE.JAZZ Series #27 featuring Greg Rodman"
      }
    ],
