    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DATE: Sunday, March 7, 2021  TIME: 7:00 pm – 8:30 pm EST  VENUE (Curbside Pickup): Club 55 - 3 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake                                            Plush Imperial - 4683 Crysler Ave Niagara Falls                                            Fiorentina - 463 Danforth Ave, Toronto  PRICE: Dinner (Curbside Pickup) and Livestreamed Show: $29 - $39 + HST (Limited number of tickets available)               Livestreamed Show (Regular price): $19 + HST               Livestreamed Show (Discount for Artists, Arts workers, and Students): $9 + HST               Season Pass (7 Shows): $99 + HST (Show Only), $249 + HST (Dinner and Show)    BUY SHOW TICKETBUY CLUB 55 TICKETBUY PLUSH IMPERIAL TICKETBUY FIORENTINA TICKETBUY SEASON PASSSEE MENU  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE SHOW  Somewhere in the night a melody spills out of a smokey alley and bounces down the cobblestone. That’s where you’ll find Dizzy &amp; Fay; through the secret door in your heart, singing love songs to the American Songbook.    In the past year, creators Mark Lalama and Amanda Walther have co-written a grand collection of original jazz songs that echo timeless standards. Think late nights, jazz cigarettes, AMSRomance and songs you swear you’ve loved your whole life. Dizzy &amp; Fay’s debut single I Wish That You Were Here drops November 20 2020, with a 12 song LP album shortly behind, arriving in 2021.    Baby, this has just begun…    Please note: All shows are currently ONLINE.  When the Province opens up and we are permitted to have gatherings in restaurants this show will take place at Club 55. Dinner and Show Season's Pass holders will have first right of refusal for a seat/table in the venue. Keep an eye on this page for updates.    DINNER + SHOW: A member of the TD Niagara Jazz Festival team will be contacting you to confirm your curbside pickup time for the evening.    LIVESTREAM: The private YouTube link will be sent to you via email on the day of the show. If you would like to see the show AFTER the air date you can purchase the 'show only' ticket and the link will be sent to you for you to view at your convenience.        ABOUT THE ARTISTS  This session of the Twilight Jazz Series features DIZZY AND FAY, with an opening performance by CYNTHIA FAY.  VIEW FULL SEASON HERE  DIZZY AND FAY      Somewhere in the night a melody spills out of a smokey alley and bounces down the cobblestone. That’s where you’ll find Dizzy &amp; Fay; through the secret door in your heart, singing love songs to the American Songbook.    In the past year, creators Mark Lalama and Amanda Walther have co-written a grand collection of original jazz songs that echo timeless standards. Think late nights, jazz cigarettes, AMSRomance and songs you swear you’ve loved your whole life. Dizzy &amp; Fay’s debut single I Wish That You Were Here drops November 20 2020, with a 12 song LP album shortly behind, arriving in 2021.    Baby, this has just begun…    Mark Lalama is an acclaimed pianist/producer/writer who has worked with some of the top Canadian jazz artists including legends like Jackie Richardson, Marc Jordan, Guido Basso, and Molly Johnson.    Amanda Walther is a Juno nominated singer-songwriter and has spent most of her career as half of the award winning folk-roots duo Dala.  CYNTHIA FAY      Cynthia Fay is a soul, folk, RnB, jazz, influenced singer songwriter. She started singing and songwriting in high school, and released her first EP at the age 16. She has performed in various places in and around Toronto including the Danforth music hall, Nathan Philips square, and she performed in a concert she put together on August 5th in Sarnia Ontario with her band, “Cynthia Fay &amp; Friends”. Cynthia was a winner of the TD Niagara Jazz Festival's JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Competition in 2017, and her band was a runner-up in the 2018 Youth Competition.          MENU        Club 55  Niagara-on-the-Lake  Price: $39 + HST  Two Course Menu  Main course  Your choice of:  Butter Chicken and Basmati        Coconut Curry Shrimp on Fragrant Basmati          Steak, Mashed Potatoes, and Green Beans with Compound Butter  Dessert  Your choice of:  Personal New York Style Cheesecake          Individual Chocolate Lava Cake with Caramel Drizzle            Plush Imperial  Niagara Falls  Price: See menu options  All dinner options come with Patacons (Spanish Chips)  Main course  Your choice of:  Jerk Chicken  Dinner Only: $29 + HST - With Dessert: $39 + HST        Vegetable Medley  Dinner Only: $29 + HST - With Dessert: $39 + HST        Curry Chicken  Dinner Only: $33 + HST - With Dessert: $39 + HST        Red Snapper  Dinner Only: $33 + HST - With Dessert: $39 + HST          Salmon  Dinner Only: $33 + HST - With Dessert: $39 + HST  Dessert  Your choice of (for an additional fee):  Black Rum Cake        Rum Raisin Bread Pudding          Coconut Cake with Key Lime Glaze            Fiorentina  Toronto  Price: $39 + HST  Three Course Menu  Appetizer  Curried Carrot and Ginger Soup   Pumpkin Seeds, Sprouts and Coconut Crème Fraiche        Main Course  Your choice of:  Vegetable Pithivier  Seasonal Vegetables in Puff Pastry  Duck Confit  Duck Fat Roasted Root Vegetables and Sauteed Greens        Dessert  Apple Pie  Brandied Crème Anglaise          BUY SHOW TICKETBUY CLUB 55 TICKETBUY PLUSH IMPERIAL TICKETBUY FIORENTINA TICKETBUY SEASON PASS          ABOUT THE TWILIGHT JAZZ SERIES    The Shea D Duo (Peter Shea + Juliet Dunn - co-creators of the TD Niagara Jazz Festival) introduced the Twilight Jazz Series to the Niagara Scene in October of 2011. The series features a different jazz ensemble the first Sunday of every month at Mahtay Café and Lounge from 6pm – 9pm focusing on Niagara musicians as well as featured musicians from Hamilton and Toronto.    Some of the past Twilight Jazz performers include: John Sherwood, James Bryan, Barbra Lica, Graham Lear, Reg Schwager, Ashley St. Pierre, Mike Murley, Jim Casson, Heilig Manoeuvre, Kevin Breit, Poco Latino, Kevin Turcotte, Rodger Niznik, Ori Dagan, John Neudorf and many more.    With the TD Niagara Jazz Festival and the ongoing Twilight Jazz Series Juliet Dunn and Peter Shea are thrilled to be able to bring live jazz to the Niagara music scene year-round.  BACK TO TOP  Proud Sponsors of the Twilight Jazz Series  [rev_slider alias=&quot;sponsors-1&quot;][/rev_slider]"
      }
    ],
