    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DATE: Thursday, October 22, 2015  TIME: 4:00 pm – 5:00 pm  VENUE: Mandeville Theatre, Ridley College, St. Catharines, ON  PRICE: FREE    To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE SHOW  Presented by the Ridley College Music Department and the TD Niagara Jazz Festival  Brian Katz is an internationally acclaimed guitarist, pianist, recording artist, improviser, composer, and music educator. The aim of this workshop is to introduce and enlighten students further to the amazing world of jazz music. Students will learn through authentic music making with Brian, one of Canada’s very best improvisational guitarists and pianists. Niagara based jazz musicians Peter Shea (Artistic Director of the TD NJF) and Juliet Dunn (Executive Director of the TD NJF) would like to grow the Jazz Festival through education opportunities presented in the public.    BE PREPARED TO MOVE, SING, SCAT, AND SWING!  Instrument is optional.    To register, please email: scott_vernon@ridleycollege.com by October 20th.  Space for participants is limited. Onlookers are welcome in the audience.    RIDLEYCOLLEGE.COM    "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
