    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Did you miss the show? You can still see it for a 50% reduced ticket price. Get your ticket today! Use Promo Code: DONTMISSGSB2021  📅 DATE: Sunday, March 28, 2021 (Or on your own time)  🕑 TIME: 11:30 am – 2:00 pm EST (Or on your own time)  🏟️ VENUE: ONLINE (livestreamed) event with curb side pickup for Brunch options  💵 PRICE: $19 Show Only ($9 for Artists, Arts Workers, and Students), $29-$39 Brunch and Show; add $20 for VIP Experience (ticket prices subject to HST)    BUY TICKETSEE MENUS AND BUY BRUNCH &amp; SHOW TICKETS  &nbsp;        ABOUT THE SHOW  We all need inspiration in these times and an uplifting Gospel Soul Brunch will do just that!    Gospel music has been woven through and into popular music for generations as the foundation for music genres such as Jazz, Blues, Country &amp; R&amp;B/Soul. The TD Niagara Jazz Festival celebrates this genre by featuring some of Canada’s emerging Gospel singers &amp; songwriters.    On March 28th, come enjoy great cuisine and the soul stirring sounds of Covenant Award nominee Jennifer Lewin &amp; the powerhouse vocals of W10 (The Williams Family) with opening act Keturah and Jonathan Morris.    Tribute to AMOY LEVY        Blessed with a unique voice, Gospel singer Amoy Levy shared her talents through her roles as director, vocal arranger, and lead vocalist with the Youth Outreach Mass Choir. Her career led her to tour across Canada and the United States, performing alongside artists such as Celine Dion, Michael Bolton, Olivia Newton-John, and Tom Cochrane, as well as Gospel greats like the Toronto Mass Choir, Danny Brooks, Ken Whiteley, and more. The world lost Amoy Levy on December 28th, 2020.    This event is a tribute to Amoy Levy.    RIP Amoy - 1970 - 2020    Please note:  A portion of the proceeds of this event will be donated to the Lupus Foundation of Canada in honour of Amoy Levy.  Thank you for your support.    &nbsp;    This show is ONLINE.     LIVESTREAM: The private YouTube link will be sent to you via email on the day before the show and on the morning of the of the show. If you would like to see the show AFTER the air date you can purchase the ‘show only’ ticket and the link will be sent to you for you to view at your convenience.    Due to the nature of unlisted videos, the performance may not be accessible through the YouTube smartphone or smart TV application (which requires videos to be listed to access). To watch this performance on devices, please use the provided link or QR code, or enter the URL directly into your device’s internet browser.    BRUNCH CUSTOMERS: Please select a Brunch pickup time during your meal selection to let the restaurant know when you will be arriving to collect your food. The available times are: 10:00 am, 10:15 am, 10:30 am, 10:45 am, and 11:00 am.    FIORENTINA Customers: As this show is scheduled for tomorrow morning, please contact the restaurant directly to place your order and purchase you 'show only' ticket here.    VIP Experience: For an additional $20, you will receive a TD Niagara Jazz Festival swag package, a gift certificate to a local restaurant partner (closest to where you live), and a virtual meet and greet with the artists and festival co-creators after the show!    &nbsp;            SUPPORT THE FESTIVAL      Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!        ABOUT THE ARTISTS  Our Gospel Soul Brunch features JENNIFER LEWIN and W10 with an opening performance by KETURAH MORRIS!  JENNIFER LEWIN      Jennifer Lewin is a passionate writer/arranger/musician/vocalist who has devoted her music to helping people find peace, hope and a relationship with God from the tender age of 6. She began her journey in a children’s choir and has served in ministry since then. Jennifer’s main goal to impact people with her music to uplift them, reassuring them that no matter how low they may feel at times, there is hope! Jennifer is a wife, mother, mentor and founder of “Nay- O – Me” Networks, a mentorship program for young women, an independent GMA Canada Nominated and International Award-winning artist, entrepreneur, ordained pastor and founder of Worship Without Walls, a weekly street ministry music, worship experience. Above all of that; she is a servant who is working very hard to get the messages of love and restoration out to as many as possible.    &nbsp;  W10      W10 is an anointed vocal group consisting of 10 biological siblings. W10 are children of the honorable Bishop and the late Lady Williams of the Abiezer Pentecostal Church. They all encompass various talents that include but are not limited to singing or playing a musical instrument.    The Siblings were born in Toronto, Canada. They all began singing at an early age in church choirs and over the years ventured into various musical journeys individually. In 2017, The family decided to release their own music and began the process of writing and recording their music.    W10 holds strong to their family vision that a family that prays together will stay together. This was the inspiration to their first single, “A Family that Prays”, which was released in February 2018. As God continues to direct them, they realize that the best is yet to come. With a vision to spread the gospel across the Globe; W10 anticipates the move of God that will shift them to the next level.    The drive to create their music project stemmed from the passing of their eldest sister and their beloved mother within a 13 month span of each other, between May 2017 and June 2018.  KETURAH MORRIS      Keturah was born into a family that was birthed into ministry and music. She has had the privilege to grow up experiencing music in the church sphere all of her life. This ultimately helped develop the gift and passion for music in her life so much so that she began utilizing it in and out of church. She is the Musical director at her church in which she directs the different choirs and leads Praise and Worship. She has also had the privilege to sing for and with several recording artists, perform live at Massey Hall for thousands, perform at charity events, weddings and much more. But with all that, her heart and love for music will always flow back to God for he is the one who makes it all possible. God is allowing her to be able to do much more things for the kingdom that has yet to be seen, so stay tuned!        MENUS  Visit our new Menus page to see our Gospel Soul Brunch offerings:  SEE MENUS  Proud Sponsors of the Gospel Soul Brunch  [rev_slider alias=&quot;GSB-sponsors-2021&quot;][/rev_slider]"
      }
    ],
