    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/master-class-part-1-new-orleans-piano-and-its-history/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/master-class-part-1-new-orleans-piano-and-its-history/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Saturday, June 12, 2021  🕑 TIME: 2:00 pm – 3:30 pm  🏟️ VENUE: Livestreamed online  💵 PRICE: FREE    CLICK HERE TO REGISTER  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE MASTER CLASS  Lance is an internationally recognized pianist and producer. One of his specialties is N’Orleans piano and the history of the players who made the style. The master class will look into both the history and the performances of Jelly Roll Morton, Tuts Washington, Prof. Longhair. Huey ‘Piano’ Smith, Allen Toussaint, Fats Domino, James Booker, Dr. John and Jon Cleary. There is a common tradition and musical well that all these performers have drawn upon to create what we now call ’N’Orleans Piano’.    This master class will be for both the pianist interested in the different styles of N’Orleans piano playing and the music fan that would like a deeper understanding of what is the foundation of so much music through the years. From second line to Blues Rumba, R&amp;B to Jazz on Frenchmen’s Street. The music of New Orleans is a GUMBO of all the influences that make the Crescent City one of the most unique and vital music communities in the world.    Lance has performed and/or recorded with Shakura S’Aida, MATCHEDASH PARISH, Maple Blues Band, Fathead, Anderson &amp; Sloski, Roger Whittaker, Deanna Bogart, Quisha Wint, Chuck Jackson, Harrison Kennedy, Jesse O’Brien, Ian Gillan, Roly Platt, Shawn Kellerman, 2B3 The Toronto Sessions and many more …"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Master Class - Part 1: New Orleans Piano and Its History"
      }
    ],
