      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Tuesday, June 29, 2021  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 8:00 pm  🏟️ VENUE: Livestreamed online  💵 PRICE: FREE    WATCH ON FACEBOOKWATCH ON YOUTUBE  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE SHOW  We will continue the countdown to Niagara's Summer Mardi Gras with this interactive, livestreamed presentation by our special guest host, Witchdoctor Utu who will be sharing his knowledge and experience with New Orleans' cultural and voodoo history.    Witchdoctor Utu is an author, the founder of the Dragon Ritual Drummers, the Niagara Voodoo Shrine, and is a member of the New Orleans Voodoo Spiritual Temple. For the last eighteen years he has been immersed in the rootwork, conjure, and mysticism surrounding the lore and legacy of the Underground Railroad. Living in St. Catharines Ontario, where Harriet “Mama Moses” Tubman brought her “track” to its end, he has been upfront and integral over the last decade by continuing to uplift and elevate the spirit of Mama Moses and her surrounding spiritual court.  Utu has also been passionately teaching animal magic through lectures, rituals, and curio methods for ten years. He travels extensively in both Canada and the United States to teach, lecture, and facilitate rituals at some of the largest spiritual gatherings on the continent.    Learn more about Witchdoctor Utu online:  www.facebook.com/witchdoctor.utu"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Mardi Gras Sessions: Exploring New Orleans Culture %26 Voodoo"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ]
