    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Friday, October 1, 2021  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 9:30 pm (Doors open at 6:00 pm)  🏟️ VENUE: Secret location in St. Catharines, North End  💵 PRICE: Show Only: $49; Charcuterie Box and Show: $69; Dinner and Show: $99 (plus HST on all prices) - The performance will proceed rain or shine. Tickets are non-refundable.    BUY TICKETSMENU  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE SHOW  Live in-person music is returning to the backyard!    Join us on Friday, October 1st with the Denielle Bassels Trio, featuring Denielle Bassels on vocals, Julien Bradley Combs on guitar, and Russ Boswell on upright bass!    Enjoy this LIVE IN-PERSON show for $49 + HST, or complete your evening with our Dinner and Show ticket for $99 + HST (meals provided by Portside Social Bar &amp; Kitchen). Show and Chacuterie Board tickets are also available for $69 + HST. Bring up to six members of your household with our VIP Tent seating (Dinner and Show) for $529 and $559.    Ticket quantities are limited, so buy yours today! For more details and to purchase tickets, visit our website at niagarajazzfestival.com    The performance will proceed rain or shine. Tickets are non-refundable.    This performance is supported by TD Bank, JAZZAMCO, DJB, Winemaker's Vintage, Stratus Vineyards, LandPro, Michael Sommer, The Loverly Co., Desjardins, CHZ PLZ, Portside Social Bar &amp; Kitchen, Anchor Pointe, and Stamford Estates.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  DENIELLE BASSELS      Indie-Swing chanteuse and bandleader Denielle DeLange (Bassels) hails from Toronto ON. Her original music whimsically weaves a caravan of influences from her childhood and travels abroad from folk and blues, to Parisian jazz manouche and swing. Denielle's original music has been described as “Ella Fitzgerald sipping tea on a rollercoaster with the Mad Hatter”. Denielle’s voice is as pure and rich as her performance style. She will immerse you in her tales. Denielle will be joined by Julien Bradley Combs on guitar and Russ Boswell on upright bass.    Denielle will be performing an intimate set of jazz standards with some of her original compositions from What About Wool Wishbags as well as from her upcoming album.  PAYPAL LINK - paypal.me/deniellebassels  RUSS BOSWELL      Russ Boswell has toured and/or recorded with some of Canada’s top artists including Corey Hart, David Wilcox, Serena Ryder, The Parachute Club, Colm Wilkinson, Seals and Crofts (USA),  Holly Cole, Dianne Tell, Ian Thomas, Marc Jordan and many others. His theatre credits include Come From Away, The Last Ship featuring Sting, Kinky Boots, Rock of Ages, Joseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat, Hair! and Tommy.  JULIEN BRADLEY-COMBS      Julien Bradley-Combs is a promising Toronto-based guitarist and composer. He has recently completed his Bachelors degree in Music, with Honours, from Humber College where he was the recipient of the Yamaha Music Award and the Musicounts Award.  Julien is a regular performer around Toronto and Southern Ontario, and plays a variety of musical genres. He has performed in several local jazz festivals (Toronto Jazz fest, Niagara Jazz Fest, Kensington Market Jazz Fest, Orangeville Jazz Fest), as well as at Toronto venues such as The Rex Hotel, The Home Smith Bar, The Emmet Ray, 120 Diner, and many others. Julien has performed with many acclaimed musicians, such as Christian McBride and Emilie-Claire Barlow during their residencies at Humber College, Ted Quinlan, Vaughan Meisner and Drew Jurecka.          MENU  Appetizer (Provided by CHZ PLZ)  Cheese and Charcuterie box for 1  (Vegan, Vegetarian and Gluten Free option also available)    Main (Choose One) (Provided by Portside Social Kitchen &amp; Bar)  Sautéed Shrimp - Garlic herb butter, sautéed shrimp, basmati rice, seasonal veg, creamy lemon butter sauce  Pollo Pesto - Penne, grilled chicken, basil pesto cream sauce, mushrooms, roasted red peppers, garlic bread  Tortellini - Cheese tortellini with sun dried tomato, pesto cream sauce, spinach, goat cheese, garlic bread (Vegetarian option)    Dessert (Choose One) (Provided by Sara's Sweets)  Mini salted caramel cheesecakes  White chocolate pumpkin blondies                CHACUTERIE CONTENTS:      2 artisan cheeses    2 local meats    House-made pickles    Preserves &amp; jams    Fresh and dried fruit    Fresh Baguette  "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Your Own Backyard Dinner and Show: Denielle Bassels Trio"
      }
    ],
