      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Saturday, July 23, 2022  🕑 TIME: 1:00 pm – 4:00 pm  🏟️ VENUE: The Brown Homestead  🗺️ ADDRESS: 1317 Pelham Rd, St. Catharines, ON L2R 6P7  💵 PRICE: Lunch &amp; Show: $99; Musicians/Arts Workers/Students SAVE 40% with Promo Code: THEMAWS2022  - Buy Now!   FOOD:  Food provided by Mahtay Café &amp; Lounge; See menu below  BUY TICKETS (Includes Picnic)ARTISTSHEALTH AND SAFETY2022 SUMMER FESTIVAL  Menu:      Cheese and Charcuterie box (Vegan and Gluten free options available)    Veggies and hummous    Sandwich (Choice of salmon / deconstructed egg sandwich on multigrain bread / cheddar with ham, lettuce &amp; tomato / veggie)    Garden salad (Lettuce, tomato, cucumber, broccoli, green apple with a lemon &amp; cumin vinaigrette) Dessert (Choice of pumpkin Choc chip loaf (Vegan) / butter pecan square / Nanaimo bar)    Seltzer water (Choice of cucumber, lemongrass, lime / Black cherry, vanilla)    Make sure you select your Menu choices for JAZZ PIC NIC by CLICKING HERE.  Generously sponsored by the Humenuik Foundation    Hosted by The Brown Homestead and Mahtay Café &amp; Market                      ABOUT THE SHOW  The evening's performance will feature Tia Brazda.    Tickets: Physical / digital tickets are not issued for this show. Admission is tracked through the order placed, and will be added to the event's guest list. Please retain your Order Confirmation email in case proof of purchase is required.    Lunch &amp; Show will have assigned seating.    Tickets are non-refundable. Artists and venues are subject to change. Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  One of Canada's most recognizable voices in jazz, Tia Brazda's jazz-pop gems and retro style have established her as a sparkling presence on the jazz scene at home and abroad, paying homage to the golden era while adding a modern twist. Having honed her cutting-edge sound in the clubs of Toronto, she burst onto the scene in 2012, hitting #1 on the iTunes Canada Jazz Chart as well as receiving play on BBC Radio 6, CBC Radio, Jazz FM 91.1 in Toronto and college radio stations across Canada. This debut brought her to Paris and Amsterdam as well as cities around the UK in support, in addition to performing at major festivals at home across Canada.    In 2015 Tia followed up with her debut full-length album 'Bandshell', which also debuted at #1 on the iTunes Jazz Chart and #3 on the Nielsen Soundscan Chart in Canada. It was also ranked the #5 best Canadian jazz release of 2015 by Jazz FM 91 in Toronto. The album also hit #24 on the CMJ national radio chart in the U.S. after being added to over 35 stations nationwide.    &nbsp;      To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!"
      }
    ],
