    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Sunday, July 24, 2022  🕑 TIME: 6:00 pm – 9:00 pm  🏟️ VENUE: The Irish Harp  🗺️ ADDRESS: 245 King St, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON L0S 1J0  💵 PRICE: FREE      ARTISTSABOUT THE SERIESHEALTH AND SAFETY  &nbsp;  Hosted by The Irish Harp          ABOUT THE SHOW  The evening's performance will feature the TBA Trio.      Thomas Reid on Drums    Bradley Krauss on Guitar    Adrian Juras on Bass    Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.    &nbsp;        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  THOMAS REID      Born and raised in Niagara, Thomas studied jazz performance at McGill University. After which he began to touring through New York, Eastern Canada and the Eastern Caribbean before landing in Sydney Australia.    Settling in Newcastle New South Wales, he played and recorded with top Australian musicians including Andy Firth, Adam Miller, Galapagos Duck’s Wil Sargisson and electro act “Fox Control”.    He has returned to Niagara after touring and teaching in Australia to return to his roots, playing with some of this regions finest musicians.    &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;  BRADLEY KRAUSS      Bradley Krauss is a professional musician residing in the Niagara Region. Fluent on the piano as well as the guitar, he prefers the latter to convey his contemporary influenced modern jazz style. He has performed around Ontario with various different touring acts and has just released his debut recording, The Brad Krauss EP, featuring 5 original compositions. Brad can be found gigging and promoting his own material in the Niagara region, as a member of the Thomas Nelson Band or as a duo with Chuck Jackson – vocalist for the legendary Downchild Blues Band.    &nbsp;    &nbsp;  ADRIAN JURAS      Adrian Juras is a professional bass player residing in the Niagara Region. Fluent on both Double Bass and Bass Guitar, he has performed around North America with various different touring acts and worked for Carnival Cruise Lines entertainment in the Caribbean. You will find Adrian most often performing in production shows, theaters, as well as freelancing around Niagara and the GTA in various Jazz, R&amp;B, Country, and Singer/Songwriter settings.    &nbsp;        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!"
      }
    ],
