    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅 DATE: Monday, June 5th, 2023  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️ VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON L0S 1J0  💵 PRICE: $39 + HST  💵 DISCOUNT:  MAWS (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students) $19 + HST  💵 SERIES PASS:  $169 (Value of $205)  🍕 FOOD:  Cheese and Charcuterie box for $20 + HST / Artisanal Pizzas for $22 + HST  (Food options available at Check Out)  🚗 PARKING: Free on site            BUY TICKETSFOOD  VIEW ALL SHOWS                      ABOUT THE SHOW:  Get ready to enjoy the sweet Rhythm and Blues of the Bentley Collective                  Presented by the TD Niagara Jazz Festival in partnership with the Hare Wine Co and co-sponsored by Aspira Heatherwood Retirement.                        This show is generously co-sponsored by Charles Climenhage of Royal Lepage.                    ABOUT THE ARTISTS:        Brooke Blackburn on Guitar and Vocals    Brooke Bentley Blackburn is the composer, singer, and guitar player behind The Bentley Collective. He has played with bands like Blackburn, Shakura S'Aida, and more. Performing for over thirty-five years, he has amassed a vast repertoire of original compositions. His solo album Songs was released in 2016. Read more.    Aubrey Dayle on Drums    At the age of 5 Aubrey started to study the accordion and piano. After completing his formal education at McGill University and Manhattan School of Music, in classical and jazz percussion,  Aubrey went on to perform in varied situations. He has toured with James ‘Blood’ Ulmer, Hassan Hakmoun (support act for Peter Gabriel), God Street wine, The John Popper Band, Sam Rivers, Ernest Ranglin and several other artists. Read more.      Roger Williams on Bass    Roger Williams is a Toronto-based, Jamaican born musician who calls on the music of his forefathers. From jazz, soul, R&amp;B and the blues, to reggae and ska, it burns through the smoking bass lines of his upright and electric basses. A highly regarded sought after musician, he has toured extensively with many artists nationally and internationally. View Artist.    Paige Armstrong on Guitar    Born in Montreal and raised in Woodview (just outside of Peterborough). Paige began studying piano at the age of nine, took up the saxophone at the age of eleven and finally the guitar at 13.  Currently living in Toronto he enjoys playing Blues, Rock, Soul, Funk, Jazz and R&amp;B. Paige has shared the stage with artists such as Buddy Guy, Eric Gales, Matt Schofield, Philip Sayce, Donna Gratis, Booker T and many more. Read more.  VIEW ALL SHOWS      FOOD:  The Hare Wine Co. is offering some delicious menu items to accompany your wine and jazz experience. A small cheese and charcuterie board for $20 + HST, as well as your choice of a 12-inch pizza for $22 + HST (Smoked duck, Pepperoni or Margarita.) Order in advance when you buy your tickets.  PLEASE NOTE:   (Food options available at Check Out)        BUY TICKETS &amp; FOOD    "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "TWILIGHT JAZZ %26 BLUES SERIES:  MONDAY NIGHT BLUES - BENTLEY COLLECTIVE"
      }
    ],
