        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Wednesday, July 19, 2023  🕑 TIME: 7:30 pm – 11:00 pm   (Doors open 1 hour before showtime)  🏟️ VENUE: Niagara Artists Centre  🗺️ ADDRESS: 354 St Paul Street, St. Catharines, ON  💵 PRICE: $29 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE: $19 + HST + Fees (MAWS Discount: Musician/ArtsWorker/Student - must show proof)  💵 PRICE: Summer Festival Full Pass: $269 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE: Weekend Pass (July 15 + 16): $139 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE: 2-Day Pass (July 20 + 21): $89 + HST + Fees  🍷 DRINKS: Cash bar on site  🥗 FOOD: $20 + HST + Fees - PRE-ORDER @ Checkout:  Small Charcuterie Boxes by CHZ PLZ!  Boxes include a serving size for 2-3 people and a selection of:      3 artisan cheeses    Genoa, Abruzze and Prosciutto&lt;    House-made pickles    Preserves &amp; jams    Fresh and dried fruit    House made Crostini on the side    Contains Nuts    NOTE: This venue is not accessible!        BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETSVIEW ALL SHOWS                              ABOUT THE SHOW:  The TD Niagara Jazz Festival is grateful to have dedicated volunteer photographers that continue to capture the essence of the festival. Spectacular moments that are frozen in time thanks to their incredible talent.    This event showcases the work of the TD Niagara Jazz Festival’s amazing photographers throughout the years.    A huge thanks to Dan Brown, Cosmo Condina, Bill Beard &amp; Jeff on Camera for all that they do.        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  The Wojtek Justyna TreeOh! fuses the energy of funk-jazz, the colors and rhythms of world music with fresh sonic explorations through combining soaring fuzzy leads with the rootsy sounds of traditional African instruments and throbbing synth bass lines. For their third album “THRICE” (2022) the musicians have joined their creative compositional talents to write a set of music that is packed with head nodding grooves, intriguing harmonies and vigorous melodies that are bound to captivate the listener.    Countless worldwide performances in clubs and renowned jazz festivals such as Jazz in Daegu (South Korea), Delft Jazz Festival, State-X New Forms, Bevrijdingsfestival (The Netherlands), Jazzmeile Thüringen, Jazzahead! (Germany) and Letni Festiwal Jazzowy (Poland) have earned the TreeOh! a reputation of an electrifying live act full of dynamics, colorful textures and fiery interplay between the band members.    Line up:      Wojtek Justyna (Poland/The Netherlands) - guitar    Szymon Justyński (Poland) - bass guitar    Alex Bernath (Germany) - drums    Diogo Carvalho (Portugal) – percussion, balafon &amp; synth    OPENING ACT  Raquel Marina will be opening for this event.  Raquel Marina was the winner in the Ages 18-23 (Solo Vocals) category in our 2023 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Competition. CLICK HERE to see their full bio.  EMCEE  This event is Emceed by Tenja Hagenberg.  Tenja Hagenberg was a judge (Vocals &amp; Vocal Coach) in our 2023 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Competition. CLICK HERE to see their full bio.        ABOUT THE PHOTOGRAPHERS:      Dan Brown    Dan Brown is a music and dance photographer based in Niagara. He’s been with the TD Niagara Jazz Festival since its inception.    CLICK HERE to see Dan's full bio.    &nbsp;        Cosmo Condina    A professional photographer since 1985, Cosmo Condina is known for his subtle, and compelling travel images. His photographic journeys have taken him across Canada, the USA, Mexico, the Caribbean, Europe, Australia and New Zealand. An associate photographer for Getty Images since 1990, Condina also is affiliated with stock agencies Alamy, Robert Harding and Stock Connection. His work is licensed for commercial and editorial use worldwide. Corporations that have used his images for advertising include American Express, Visa, United Airlines, Molson’s Brewery, Ontario Savings Bonds and Fuji Film. Condina has published three books; “Niagara on the Lake”, “Niagara at War 1812” and “Early Architecture of Niagara and the Niagara Township” His fine artwork is exhibited in many galleries, where he is represented by Oliver Gordon.    CLICK HERE to see Cosmo's full bio.    &nbsp;        Bill Beard    I have been photographing seriously since 2001 concentrating on nature and street photography. In 2012 I started my jazz  photography career taking pictures of the group Red Hot Ramble. When I retired in 2013 I started to volunteer at JAZZ.FM91 and shortly after I joined I started doing photography for them.    I have photographed for the Markham, Toronto, and Kensington Market festivals. My favourite Festival was the Niagara Jazz Festival where I got to meet such wonderful people who volunteered at the festival. I photographed two seasons of the festival. some shows at the cafe, the World Music show, and a big band show.  I can't say enough about Juliet and Peter who took me in with such warm hospitality.  They made me feel right at home and part of the festival family.    COVID put a stop to my jazz career so I have concentrated on nature, specifically birds. My images can be seen on Facebook under my name (Bill Beard).    &nbsp;        Jeff on Camera    Jeff is a Niagara based photographer whose love for the camera and music have combined in his business Jeff on Camera. For over 5 years, he’s had the privilege of shooting a variety of artists, from local musicians in small clubs to music icons in crowded stadiums. Whether it’s the Gasworks in Hamilton, or the Meridian Centre in St. Catharines, Jeff captures the energy and emotion of each performance and has the creative and technical skills to produce beautiful stage, promo and head shots. A musician himself, he anticipates the moments that translate into photos both artists and audiences love.    CLICK HERE to see Jeff's full bio.        PLEASE NOTE:      Physical/digital tickets are not issued for this show. Admission is tracked through the order placed and will be added to the event’s guest list. Please retain your Order Confirmation email in case proof of purchase is require.    Tickets are non-refundable. Artists and venues are subject to change. Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    Artists and venues subject to change.    This event will take place rain or shine.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          HOSTED BY THE NIAGARA ARTISTS CENTRE        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETSVIEW ALL SHOWS  &nbsp;  Supported in part by:  "
      }
    ],
