    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/jazz-4-the-ages-youth-contest/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/jazz-4-the-ages-youth-contest/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Registration is now open until March 15th!  Niagara Jazz Festival co-creators Juliet Dunn, and the late Peter Shea, strongly believe in mentoring and empowering youth in their community and beyond. In 2015 they started their LIVE.LEARN.JAZZ program to inspire people young and old to learn more about the art form and to get involved. Under this umbrella is a program called ‘JAZZ 4 the AGES’, an annual competition that is open to youth in the 23 and under age groups.    Auditions are curated by a panel of professional jazz musicians with expertise in the following instruments: Piano, guitar, vocals, saxophone, trumpet, flute, drums &amp; percussion, organ, producing and more.    JAZZ 4 the AGES has provided learning and performance opportunities for various young and upcoming musicians. A series of Master Class workshops are also made available for students and musicians featuring top musicians from around the globe. The festival partners with Ridley College to help bring this program to fruition.  Submissions are now open!   2025 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Program Competition   Registration closes March 15th, 2025  CLICK HERE to register  &nbsp;    More info for your audition:  1st round - Pre-selection      Please submit one YouTube video of you performing your favourite song or piece. Doesn't necessarily have to be jazz but preferred.    2nd round - Auditions      Those pre-selected from the submissions will be invited to in-person auditions at Ridley College in St. Catharines on Wednesday April 2nd, 2025.  Contrasting songs/pieces are required for the auditions and one song must be a jazz piece.  If you are a singer or solo instrumentalist (any instrument) an accompanist will be available to back you up for the performance. You must provide the name of the song in advance, and if a chart is needed for the accompanist you will need to provide the chart. If you are not from Southern Ontario, you may do a ZOOM audition for this round.    3rd round - FINALS  Those who are selected for the FINALS will audition in person at Ridley College on May 4, 2025.  Two contrasting songs/pieces will be required, and one must be a jazz piece. At minimum one piece should be different from the 1st round selections.  Winners will be announced at the end of the Finals.  All winners will have the opportunity to perform during the 2025 Niagara Jazz Festival summer season. Finalists will be invited to perform during the rest of our calendar year at events such as Twilight Jazz Series, Twilight Jazz &amp; Blues Series, and others.    AGE CATEGORIES:  11 and under, 12 - 14, 15 - 17, 18 - 23      CLICK HERE to submit            2023 JAZZ 4 the AGES Winner - Nicholas Mustapha Trio   Jackson-Triggs Amphitheatre  Niagara Jazz Festival's 10th Anniversary   Flagship event  'Jazz Under the Stars'            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2025 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Competition"
      }
    ],
