    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Monday, May 13th, 2024  🕑TIME: 7:00 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake  💵PRICE: $39 + HST + Fees  💵DISCOUNT:  $19 + HST + Fees - MAWS Discount   (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students)   🍕 FOOD: Artisanal Pizzas are available for purchase at The Hare Wine Co.  🚗 PARKING: Free on site            BUY TICKETS                    ABOUT THE SHOW:               &quot;Murmurations pre-release&quot; Montreal-based jazz pianist... More info coming soon...                          Presented by the Niagara Jazz Festival in partnership with                      ABOUT THE ARTISTS:    Kate Wyatt      Originally from Victoria BC, pianist and composer Kate Wyatt is now considered one of the top-tier jazz musicians in the city of Montreal. She has been praised as having “musical ideas and a style of playing and writing that is on par with the current jazz piano elite: Mehldau, Yaron Herman, Shai Maestro, Fred Hersch”, and has been hailed as, “one of the top artists of Montreal, Quebec, or even Canadian jazz.” (Cardin/Brunet, panm360.com)    In July 2022 Wyatt released her debut album Artifact to excellent critical reviews. Joined by Lex French (trumpet), Adrian Vedady (bass), and Jim Doxas (drums) she leads a quartet whose effortless chemistry fosters deep interaction and high intensity. As one reviewer described, “Artifact is filled with melody, spirit, and a joy for playing together that brings the listener hope. This album is a gem. Highly recommended!!” (Richard Kamins, Step Tempest)      Read more...  __________________________________________________________________________________________________________      BUY TICKETS      __________________________________________________________________________________________________________        Food Options:  The Hare Wine Co. is offering delicious menu items to accompany your wine and jazz experience. A small cheese and charcuterie board, focaccia, as well as your choice of 12-inch artisanal pizzas. Order directly from your table server the night of the show!    "
      }
    ],
