        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Screen-Shot-2024-06-07-at-4.04.12-PM.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/3rd-annual-jazz-picnic-ft-denielle-bassels/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/3rd-annual-jazz-picnic-ft-denielle-bassels/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Sunday, June 23, 2024  🕑 TIME: 1:00 pm – 4:00 pm   (Doors open 1 hour before showtime)  🏟️ VENUE:  The Brown Homestead (seating will be provided)  🗺️ ADDRESS: ON  💵 PRICE (Regular): $110 -  NOW ONLY $80 + HST + Fees (USE PROMO CODE: PICNIC-2024)  TICKET SALES CLOSE JUNE 21 @ NOON to accommodate catering time requirements)  💵 PRICE: (MAWS discount): $80 + HST + Fees   (MAWS: Musician/ArtsWorker/Student - must show proof)  💵 PRICE: VIP Summer Festival Full Pass: $229 + HST + Fees   (includes picnic lunch - Valued at $300)  🥗 FOOD: VIP Picnic Lunch included (menu and selection below)  🍷 DRINKS: Cash bar on site provided by Niagara College Teaching Winery, Brewery, Distillery and Cidery  SEATING:  Seating provided on site  🚗 PARKING: FREE on site        BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETSLUNCHVIEW ALL SHOWS            Presented by      ___________________________________________________________________________  Supported by                  ABOUT THE SHOW:  At the historic Brown Homestead, where time seems to slow to a jazz tempo, Denielle Bassels will cast her musical spell over a sun-drenched afternoon picnic. Beneath the azure sky, and underneath a billowing canopy, guests will gather to dine and dance as the sun plays hide-and-seek through the leaves. Caught in the timeless embrace of music and nature, Denielle and her band will create an afternoon symphony of serenity and joy. Every instant will blossom into a treasured, timeless tune.    Please note: Seating is provided.        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  Denielle Bassels    Toronto-born jazz vocalist and songwriter Denielle Bassels' career in music began working as an au-pair in Lausanne, Switzer- land. She started singing in clubs to earn extra money to extend her stay and incidentally found herself performing with some of the country’s top jazz musicians. &quot;We'd set up unannounced at a restaurant and begin playing, and if the patrons liked the music we would be allowed to stay. We always stayed!&quot; She performed across Switzerland and France at jazz caves and festivals for two years before returning home to Canada to pursue a deeper education in music and received her Bachelors of Music from Humber College in Toronto. In 2017 she released her debut full-length album of eleven originals“What About Wool Wishbags”, reaching #1 on the iTunes Jazz charts in Canada. Seven of these originals received international awards, including a grand prize in the “International John Lennon Songwriting Competition” for her song “Cool Cool Water”. In 2018 she was a featured vocalist on the studio album “Muse” by Jaymz Bee’s The Tiki Collective, which debuted her original song “Wanderer” alongside performances by Lily Frost, Joanna Mojoko, and The Willows. In June 2023, Bassels released her 2nd full-length original Album “Little Bit a’ Love” to rave reviews and was nominated in 2024 for a June for “Best Vocal Jazz Album of the Year”. She is currently getting ready to release her newest album for 2024 funded by FACTOR Canada.    PRAISE/QUOTES:    “Bassels has a winning combination here: a strong, clear voice, great stage presence, along with a tight rhythm section, forceful gypsy-jazz-influenced guitar, and expressive clarinet and tenor sax.” Brett Delmage, ottawajazzscene.ca    “There is something about the imaginative way in which Denielle thinks, crafts and creates music that is undeniably her own. What About Wool Wishbags is a remarkable collection of songs that brings together the past and the future with strong songwriting structures that still leave room for all sorts of adventure. 2017 has been blessed.” -Dani Elwell, JAZZ FM 91.1    For her performance, Denielle will be joined by Glenn Anderson on Drums, Eric St. Laurent on Guitar, and Rob Lee on Upright Bass.  OPENING ACT  One of our JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth winners will be opening for this performance. The youth finals are on June 2nd so the opening act will be announced after that date.  EMCEE  This event is Emceed by Walter Venafro from JAZZ.FM 91's Saturday Afternoon Jazz, Sunday Drive and Blurred Lines.  CLICK HERE to see his full bio.        PLEASE NOTE:      Seating will be provided for the Jazz Picnic    Tickets are non-refundable.    Artists and venue are subject to change    This event will take place rain or shine    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          Gourmet Picnic Lunch Partner    Picnic Box Lunch menu options:        1/2 Sandwich (Choice of 1)  Veggie Wrap with Red Pepper Hummus  Chicken Salad on a Croissant  Black Forest Ham with Swiss cheese on a White Sesame Bread    Salad Options (Choice of 1)  Mixed Greens with a Cherry Balsamic Vinaigrette  Italian Pasta Salad    Each box would contain  *2 slices of Cheese (wrapped together separately)  *Butter Cookie with a Strawberry Heart  *Grapes &amp; Strawberries    Place Your Orders HERE            Official Beverage Partner   _________________________________________________________________________________________________  In Partnership with      &nbsp;    &nbsp;      In Support ofNiagara Jazz Festival will be donating $1 per ticket sold in support of MusiCounts, starting with ticketed concert events during summer festival week from June 21-29, 2024. With events such as JAZZ 4 the AGES, on-site activations during our summer festival, and other exciting initiatives throughout the year, we are extremely excited about our new partnership with MusiCounts.  _________________________________________________________________________________________________  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETSVIEW ALL SHOWS  &nbsp;  Generously Supported by  "
      }
    ],
