    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Thursday, June 27, 2024  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 10:00 pm   (Doors open 1 hour before showtime)  🏟️ VENUE: Mandeville Theatre, Ridley College  🗺️ ADDRESS: 2 Ridley Road, St. Catharines, ON  💵 PRICE (Regular): $40 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE (MAWS Discount): $20 + HST + Fees   (MAWS: Musician/ArtsWorker/Student - must show proof)  💵 PRICE: Summer Festival Full Pass: $229 + HST + Fees   💺 SEATING:  Soft-seater theatre seating  🍷 DRINKS: Cash bar on site provided by Niagara College Teaching Winery, Brewery, Distillery and Cidery          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETS            Presented by            ABOUT THE SHOW: A Tribute to Nat 'King' Cole          ABOUT THE ARTISTS: BRYAN ENG TRIO  Celebrating the release of his new album, the Bryan Eng Trio will be performing Nat ‘King’ Cole standards along with his original compositions featured on the record. From New York City, multifaceted jazz pianist, singer, composer, and actor, Bryan Eng is one of the most promising and accomplished entertainers of his generation. With performances on Broadway, the Kennedy Center, Jazz at Lincoln Center, Birdland, and an ongoing run as the youngest resident performer ever at the esteemed Carlyle Hotel, the 25-year-old entertainer has already made his mark on the world’s most esteemed stages.    Read more...    Hear more...        OPENING ACT  One of our JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth winners will be opening for this performance. The youth finals are on June 2nd so the opening act will be announced after that date.        PLEASE NOTE:      Artists and venue are subject to change.    Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          In Partnership with      ______________________________________________________________________________________________    Official Summer Festival Beverage Partner       _________________________________________________________________________________________________  A portion of ticket sales in support of    Niagara Jazz Festival will be donating $1 per ticket sold in support of MusiCounts, starting with ticketed concert events during summer festival week from June 21-29, 2024. With events such as JAZZ 4 the AGES, on-site activations during our summer festival, and other exciting initiatives throughout the year, we are extremely excited about our new partnership with MusiCounts.        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!            BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETS  _________________________________________________________________________________________________   Generously Supported by  "
      }
