    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Friday, June 21, 2024 (RAIN or SHINE)  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 10:00 pm   (Doors open 1 hour before showtime)  🏟️ VENUE: Oakes Garden Theatre  🗺️ ADDRESS: 5825 River Rd, Niagara Falls, ON L2G 3K9  💵 PRICE (Regular): $40 + HST + Fees   💵 PRICE (MAWS Discount): $20 + HST + Fees   MAWS: Musician/ArtsWorker/Student - must show proof  MAWS  Tickets - PLEASE USE PROMO CODE: industryrate24   💵 PRICE: Summer Festival Full Pass: $229 + HST + Fees  🪑 SEATING: Bring your own lawn chair and / or blanket!   🍕SNACKS: Available on site  🍷 DRINKS: Cash bar on site             BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETS            Presented by      _________________________________________________________________________________________________  Supported by  _________________________________________________________________________________________________  In Partnership with                  ABOUT THE SHOW:  The POWER of MUSIC event stands as a testament to the vibrancy of the Black and Indigenous artists that we will be presenting. Against the stunning backdrop of Niagara Falls, Jazz and Blues music will echo stories of resilience. A magical blend of history, music, and nature. Come and join us for a summer evening in the most stunning live music venue on Earth!    CLICK HERE to hear directly from Juliet Dunn, Executive Artistic Producer of Niagara Jazz Festival        ABOUT THE ARTISTS: BLACKBURN BROTHERS  From the Blackburn Family Archives HERE        OPENING ACT: SEAN STANLEY QUARTET      The Sean Stanley Quartet PROUDLY plays Jazz, Swing and the Blues. The music of Louis Armstrong, Ray Charles and Duke Ellington as well as Sean's original compositions. Their new O.A.C. (Ontario Arts Council) funded record &quot;Quintet-isms&quot; is available on all major streaming services.    Promotional Video              OPENING ACT - 2024 JAZZ 4 the AGES Winner  Mattaus Gertzinger Quartet        PLEASE NOTE:      PARKING OPTIONS: Guide to Parking in Niagara Falls /  Niagara Parks /  Niagara Parks Parking Pass /  Clifton Hill Parking    This event will take place 'Rain or Shine'    General admission - grass seating - bring your own lawn chair/blanket    Artists and venue are subject to change.    Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          Fallsview Stage Presenter    ____________________________________________  A portion of ticket sales in support of    Niagara Jazz Festival will be donating $1 per ticket sold in support of MusiCounts, starting with ticketed concert events during summer festival week from June 21-29, 2024. With events such as JAZZ 4 the AGES, on-site activations during our summer festival, and other exciting initiatives throughout the year, we are extremely excited about our new partnership with MusiCounts.        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETS  &nbsp;  Generously Supported by  "
      }
    ],
