    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Wednesday, June 26, 2024  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 10:00 pm   (Doors open 1 hour before showtime)  🏟️ VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Road, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵 PRICE (Regular): $40 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE (MAWS Discount): $20 + HST + Fees   (MAWS: Musician/ArtsWorker/Student - must show proof)  💵 PRICE: Summer Festival Full Pass: $229 + HST + Fees    🍕 FOOD: Available for purchase on site   🍷 DRINKS: Cash bar on site      SEATING: Available on site          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETS    _________________________________________________________________  Presented by                  ABOUT THE SHOW:  JAZZ FUSION in the VINEYARD will blow you away! Montreal-based bassist Carl Mayotte and his trio will infuse the air with a captivating blend of jazz fusion for this intimate performance at the Hare Wine Co. At this beautiful venue, you will enjoy an evening filled with the rich tones of Mayotte's bass, melodic rhythms, and some of the best wines that the Niagara region has to offer!    Please note: Our shows at this venue often sell out so be sure to get your passes and/or tickets right away!        ABOUT THE ARTISTS: CARL MAYOTTE TRIO  Winner of the Félix award for Jazz Album of the Year at the ADISQ (the equivalent of the Grammy Awards in Quebec) in 2022 for his third album Escale, and recipient of the Jazz Revelation title from Radio-Canada for 2020-2021, Carl Mayotte is one of the most prominent young bassists and jazz musicians in Quebec and Canada at the moment. Having started his professional career at the age of 16 and completed a master's degree in jazz performance at McGill University, his virtuosity and versatility have been recognized by several musicians and critics, including the legendary bassist Alain Caron and the popular Bass Magazine. Additionally, in the summer of 2022, he launched a new jazz music camp in Kamouraska, bringing together musicians of all ages and skill levels. One of the young musician's goals is to democratize jazz and bring this musical genre to the forefront. In line with this objective, he has just released his first book with Hudson Music: &quot;The Ultimate Jazz Fusion Play-Along For Bass.&quot; He has just released his fourth album, Carnaval, a tribute to Brazilian music that is undoubtedly the most ambitious project of the young musician.  More about Carl Mayotte HERE        OPENING ACT  2024 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth winner - Mill Jazz Trio -  will be opening for this performance!        PLEASE NOTE:      Artists and venue are subject to change.    This event takes place indoors (Be sure to come early to enjoy a glass of wine on the outdoor patio).    Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          In Partnership with  Jennifer Poynton Desjardins Insurance      ______________________________________________________________________________________________  A portion of ticket sales in support of  Niagara Jazz Festival will be donating $1 per ticket sold in support of MusiCounts, starting with ticketed concert events during summer festival week from June 21-29, 2024. With events such as JAZZ 4 the AGES, on-site activations during our summer festival, and other exciting initiatives throughout the year, we are extremely excited about our new partnership with MusiCounts.        Click here to donate and support the Niagara Jazz Festival:    Donations to the Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETS  &nbsp;  Generously Supported by  "
      }
    ],
