    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Saturday June 29, 2024  🕑 TIME: 1:00 pm – 10:30 pm   🏟️ UPDATED VENUES: Moose and Goose (Indoors) and Donnelly's Pub (Indoors)  🗺️ ADDRESS: 54 Paul De Divitiis Senior Way, Thorold and 54 Front Street, Thorold   💵 PRICE: FREE COMMUNITY EVENT - All ages welcome!  🪑SEATING:Available on Site  🍕FOOD:Various food vendors on site    🍷DRINKS:Various beverage vendors on site                   Presented by                  ABOUT THE EVENT: NEW LOCATION! INDOORS DUE TO INCLEMENT WEATHER  This FREE event features both Jazz and World Music Artists and will take place at the Moose and Goose and Donnelly's Pub in the City of Thorold on Saturday, June 29th from 1 pm to 10:30 pm.    This event will include the following:      Live music all day long on two (2) stages - OLG Fiesta Stage &amp; Groove Garden Stage    Artisan Vendors    Food vendors    Wine, Beer, Cider,  and non-alcoholic beverages    Kids zone    VIP seating area for pass holders    Community partners    and more!    CLICK HERE to sign up and be sure to bring your lawn chair or blanket! *    * Sign up for this FREE event and be entered for a chance to win tickets for one of the Niagara Jazz Festival Fall events.        Live Music Schedule     Sat, June 29, 2024    OLG FIESTA STAGE - NOW AT MOOOSE &amp; GOOSE- 54 Paul De Divitis Senior Way (Downtown Thorold)    1 pm - 1:30 pm - Opening Remarks / Indigenous Opening    1:30 p.m. to 2:00 p.m. The Imbayakunas (International)     2:15 p.m. to 2:45 p.m.  Moon    3 p.m. to 3:45 p.m. Angela Turone + Chris Platt    4:15 p.m. to 5 p.m. Alistair Robertson Quartet    5:30 p.m. to 6:15 p.m. Heavyweights Brass Band    6:45 p.m. to 7:30 p.m. Wojtek Justyna TreeOh! (International)    8 p.m. to 9 p.m.  Malia Love    9:30 p.m. to 10:30 p.m. KIRK DIAMOND and the Movement of Ahryel     &nbsp;    GROOVE GARDEN STAGE - NOW AT DONNELLY'S PUB 54 FRONT ST. S. (Downtown Thorold)     Start Times Subject to Change!    6:15 p.m. to 6:45 p.m. Fernandha Cunha Trio    7:30 p.m. to 8:00 p.m. Fuat Tuaç Quartet    9 p.m. to 9:30 p.m  NEMESIS Duo (Scott Jackson Beatbox + Dr. Draw on electric violin)    &nbsp;    TENT TALKS - LOCATION TBC (Downtown Thorold)    Time TBC - History of the Welland Canal - Tom Russell:  Historian    Time TBC -  International Artists Meet and Greet - Imbayakunas    Time TBC -  BREAKING THE BINARY:  A poetic discussion on queer identity in Jamaica &amp; the Caribbean - Moon Artist     Time TBC - History of Black Music in Canada - Carlos Morgan:  Singer, Songwriter, Producer, Recording Artist    Time TBC -  International Artists Meet and Greet - Wojtek Justyna TreeOh!         PLEASE NOTE:      Rain or Shine    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          Supported by  _________________________________________________________________________________________________  Fiesta Stage Presenter  ____________________________________________  A portion of tickets sales in support of    Niagara Jazz Festival will be donating $1 per ticket sold in support of MusiCounts, starting with ticketed concert events during summer festival week from June 21-29, 2024. With events such as JAZZ 4 the AGES, on-site activations during our summer festival, and other exciting initiatives throughout the year, we are extremely excited about our new partnership with MusiCounts.        Click here to donate and support the festival:    Donations to the Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASS  &nbsp;  Supported in part by:  "
      }
