    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅 DATE: Friday, June 28, 2024  🕑 TIME: 1:00 pm - 3:30 pm  🏟️ VENUE: Ridley College (Chapel)  🗺️ ADDRESS:  2 Ridley Road, St. Catharines, ON  💵 PRICE: Students FREE  / Everyone Welcome 'Pay What You Can'           SIGN UP / BUY TICKETS            Presented by            ABOUT THE MASTER CLASS:  “Anatomy of a Tune” Masterclass with the Wojtek Justyna TreeOh!    Expand your listening skills and deepen your appreciation of music while gaining insights into the creative process.    From the initial spark of inspiration to the final notes performed on stage, Wojtek Justyna TreeOh! will illuminate every step of the musical journey by breaking down one of their compositions. Participants will discover the secrets behind crafting memorable melodies, intricate harmonies, and dynamic arrangements.    Join us for this immersive experience that will enrich your musical world, ignite your creativity, and empower you with the tools to enjoy and make music on a higher level.          ABOUT THE ARTIST: WOJTEK JUSTYNA TREEOH!  The Wojtek Justyna TreeOh! fuses the energy of funk-jazz, the colors and rhythms of world music with fresh sonic explorations through combining soaring fuzzy leads with the rootsy sounds of traditional African instruments and throbbing synth bass lines. These multinational musicians have joined their creative compositional talents to write music that is packed with head nodding grooves, intriguing harmonies and vigorous melodies that are bound to captivate the listener.    Countless worldwide performances, with their three deliciously grooving studio albums, in clubs and renowned jazz festivals such as Niagara Jazz Festival (Canada), Kolkata Jazzfest (India), Jazz in Daegu (South Korea), Jazz in Duke Town (The Netherlands), Jazzahead! (Germany) and Letni Festiwal Jazzowy (Poland) have earned the TreeOh! a reputation of an electrifying live act full of dynamics, colorful textures and fiery interplay between the band members.    Line Up:    Wojtek Justyna (Poland/The Netherlands) - guitar  Daniel Lottersberger (Austria) - bass guitar  Alex Bernath (Germany) - drums  Maxim Zettel (Germany) – percussion                    PLEASE NOTE:                  Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          In Partnership with    ____________________________________________  Supported by  _________________________________________________________________________________________________  Supported by      _________________________________________________________________________________________________  A portion of tickets sales in support of    Niagara Jazz Festival will be donating $1 per ticket sold in support of MusiCounts, starting with ticketed concert events during summer festival week from June 21-29, 2024. With events such as JAZZ 4 the AGES, on-site activations during our summer festival, and other exciting initiatives throughout the year, we are extremely excited about our new partnership with MusiCounts.        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!            SIGN UP / BUY TICKETS    _________________________________________________________________________________________________      Supported in part by    "
      }
    ],
