      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Saturday June 22, 2024  🕑 TIME: 3 pm – 6 pm  🏟️ VENUE: Lakeview Winery  🗺️ ADDRESS: 1067 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON L0S 1J0  💵 PRICE: FREE COMMUNITY EVENT  💵 Summer Festival Full Pass: $229 + HST + Fees  🪑 SEATING: Available on site  🍕SNACKS: Available on site  🍷 WINE: Available on site                ABOUT THE EVENT:      Catch a FREE Pop-up show with the Niagara Jazz Festival one Saturday, June 22. Visit us at one of our venue partners across the Niagara Region and enjoy live jazz with your outing.  Featuring some of Ontario's finest jazz talent. Enjoy some of Niagara's finest wine while you enjoy live music in the vineyard. Festival Co-Creator Juliet Dunn will introduce the show and will be on site!  Come out and say hi!        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:          South Coast Jazz Founder/Producer    Juliann’s career has been shaped by over 30 years of professional training and experience in front and behind the scenes as a professional, nationally ranked dancer, vocalist, actor, director, producer, choreographer, certified personal trainer, yoga and dance instructor. Her training includes Broadway Dance Center, Steps, Alvin Ailey-NYC, Ichibangai-Japan, Edge-LA, New England Conservatory-Boston and Sheridan College-ON.                  Juliann has performed, produced, consulted and directed countless shows and programs world-wide. Since the release of her five recordings including: Compotion 2001 (Europe) Don’t Explain 2010 (Bill King Producer) and self produced Broken Compass 2012, Blue Girl Green 2013, A Good Jazz Collection 2018 (EQMusic), Juliann has established record distribution deals in Singapore, Thailand, Malaysia, Japan, and has charted internationally reaching #1 and #2 on major radio charts, won Best New Artist/original  music at Barrie Music Festival, opened Canadian Music Week Jazz Showcase, performed at Mont Tremblant/Toronto Jazz/Celebrate Toronto and Niagara Jazz Festivals’ and has been showcased on over 225 radio stations.                  Selected stage includes: Cats-Germany, Joseph and the Amazing Technicolour Dreamcoat-National tour with Donny Osmond, Beauty and the Beast-Japan. Select film/TV credits include: DaVinci’s Inquest, First Wave, The Prize Winner Of Defiance Ohio-Woody Harrelson/Julianne Moore/Laura Dern, MOW Martin and Lewis with Sean Hayes. Juliann’s now producing music and TV and Video-On-Demand content for herself and other artists and platforms.    To come full circle after a career abroad and eleven years making South Coast Jazz an internationally acclaimed festival, and be able to now produce world-class productions for Norfolk County and in her home town of Brantford, is truly special.  “Come make a memory that will last a lifetime, and enjoy the music.”                      In Partnership with      Lakeview Wine Co.  Located in the heart of Niagara-on-the-Lake, Lakeview Wine Co. is home to a wide selection of award winning VQA wines. Our winery produces Ontario's top-selling wine brands, including EastDell, 20 Bees and our signature Lakeview Wine. Co celebrating old world wines crafted in a new world style. To produce our wines, we source grapes from over 25 Niagara grape growing families.    Learn More About Lakeview Wine Co. »      &nbsp;               Presented by  &nbsp;      Click here to donate and support the festival:    Donations to the Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASS  &nbsp;  Supported in part by:  "
      }
    ],
