    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Saturday, November 23rd, 2024    🏟️VENUE #1 : The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Road, Niagara-on-the-Lake  🕑TIME: 11:00 am – 4:30 pm    🏟️VENUE #2 : Niagara-on-the-Lake Golf Club   🗺️ADDRESS: 143 Front Street, Niagara-on-the-Lake   🕑TIME: 2:00 pm - 7:00 pm    🏟️VENUE #3 : Queen's Landing - Bacchus Lounge  🗺️ADDRESS: 155 Byron St, Niagara-on-the-Lake  🕑TIME: 3:30 pm - 9:00 pm    💵PRICE: FREE (Regular)  💵PRICE: $19 + HST (VIP Passport*)  🍕 FOOD: Varies from Venue to venue  🚗 PARKING: Free on site (Shuttle will be running between the venues all day)    * VIP Passports include:  SOLD OUT!  - Priority boarding on the JAZZ CRAWL Shuttle   - Reserved VIP seating at each venue  - Swag bag  - 25% Discount for Twilight Jazz &amp; Blues Series (Select dates from Dec '24 - June '25)          ABOUT THE JAZZ CRAWL:      Niagara Jazz Festival presents its 2024 JAZZ CRAWL.   This exciting and FREE event invites music lovers to explore three distinct venues across the picturesque town of Niagara-on-the-Lake, enjoying live performances from 15 diverse jazz duos, trios, and quartets. Some of the confirmed artists include multi-award winner Heather Bambrick, JUNO award-winner Sammy Jackson, Doug Mundy Trio, Carolyn Credico Duo, Rodman Rodgers &amp; Moore Jazz Trio, Bradley Krauss Trio and others to be announced shortly!    With a complimentary shuttle service connecting all locations, guests can effortlessly hop between venues while soaking in the vibrant jazz scene and the scenic beauty of wine country. It's a perfect way to experience the rich culture and charm of Niagara-on-the-Lake through a weekend of exceptional music, wine, craft beer, spirits, and culinary delights.      Supported by: TD Ready Commitment, ON Creates, and the Town of Niagara-on-the-Lake      In Partnership with the Niagara-on-the-Lake Chamber of Commerce, Tourism Niagara-on-the-Lake, and the Community Transport Group.                        PERFORMANCE SCHEDULE:    The Hare Wine Co. - 769 Niagara Stone Road, NOTL  11:00 am - 11:30 am -  JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth performers - TBA    11:45 am - 12:15 pm - Doug Mundy Trio    12:45 pm - 1:15 pm - Anthony &amp; Jennarie: 'A Musical Friendship'    2:00 pm - 3:00 pm - Bill McBirnie Trio    3:30 pm - 4:30 pm - Heather Bambrick Trio  NOTL Golf Club - 143 Front Street, NOTL    2:00 pm - 2:30 pm - JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Performer - Carly Greavette (Solo Guitarist)    3:00 pm - 4:00 pm - Carolyn Credico Duo    4:30 pm - 5:30 pm - James Gay Duo    6:00 pm - 7:00 pm - Bryan Covey Trio  Queen's Landing - Bacchus Lounge - 155 Byron Street, NOTL  3:30 pm - 4:00 pm - JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Performer - Emilio Geremia    4:30 pm - 5:15 pm - Rob Fekete Trio    5:45 pm - 6;30 pm - Bradley Krauss Trio    7:00 pm - 7:45 pm - Sammy Jackson Duo    8:15 pm - 9:00 pm - Rodman, Rogers &amp; Moore Trio            Parking/Shuttle - 'Old Harvest Barn' - 1822 Niagara Stone Road, NOTL  Full Shuttle Schedule:  10:30 am first departure   10:45 am second departure   Every 30 minutes 11:00 am - 9:00 pm  &nbsp;          Presented by Niagara Jazz Festival with support from  &nbsp;                                                                                                                                       Event Sponsor                                                                                                                                Shuttle Sponsor      Shuttle Parking Sponsor     In-Kind Sponsors                  &nbsp;        &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;  Community Partners          &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;  Media Partners           &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;    &nbsp;    ___________________________________________________________________________________________________    ABOUT THE VENUES:      The Hare Wine Co. - 11 am - 4:30 pm    The Hare Wine Co. in Niagara-on-the-Lake is known for its bold, premium wines crafted in small batches. Surrounded by scenic vineyards, it offers a rustic yet elegant setting for tastings and events.  This beautiful winery is a long-time sponsor and partner of the Niagara Jazz Festival. The Hare Wine Co has been a long-time supporter of the Niagara Jazz Festival, and this JAZZ CRAWL promises an extraordinary lineup. Don’t miss the chance to enjoy their delicious wines, tasty treats, and performances from talented piano-based* duos, trios, and quartets.    Notes:      Acoustic Grand piano on site    Official Shuttle stop    Free parking lot    Accessible venue                  Niagara-on-the-Lake Golf Club - 2:00 pm - 700 pm      With the best view in town, the Niagara-on-the-Lake Golf Club, established in 1875, is North America's oldest golf course still in operation. Located on the scenic shores of Lake Ontario, this historic 9-hole course offers stunning views of the lake and Niagara River, making it a unique and picturesque spot for golfers of all skill levels.The Golf Club's dining lounge and bar are open to the public, with no membership required, making it the perfect spot to enjoy delicious food, fine wine, and the exciting concerts organized by the Niagara Jazz Festival for the JAZZ CRAWL.  Notes:      Official Shuttle stop    Free street parkin    Accessible venue                  Queen's Landing - Bacchus Lounge - 3:30 pm - 9:00 pm         From the food to the panoramic marina view, the Bacchus Lounge at Queen’s Landing is fit for the gods. Indulge in gourmet pub food, craft beer and regional wine while relaxing in comfortable leather chairs, surrounded by stained glass and classic décor, making it the perfect spot to enjoy delicious food, fine wine, and the exciting concerts organized by the Niagara Jazz Festival for the JAZZ CRAWL.  Notes:        Official Shuttle stop    Free street parking    Accessible venue    Accessible venue    "
      }
    ],
