    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATES: Monday, January 13th / Thursday February 20th / Monday March 3rd  💵 SHOWS: January Blues / Black History Month / Jazz in the Spring  🏟️VENUES: The Hare Wine Co. / Table Rock House Restaurant  🗺️ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake / 6650 Niagara Parkway, Niagara Falls  💵 SERIES PASS: $109 + HST + Fees (Includes 3 shows - does not include food)  🍕 FOOD: Available for purchase  🚗 PARKING: Free on site                    BUY PASSES                            Presented by the Niagara Jazz Festival in partnership with                          ABOUT THE SHOWS      The Johnny Max Band will perform a mix of Blues, Soul, and rhythm &amp; Blues with a few covers thrown in...Be sure to come out for the Johnny Max Band experience. Blues, to shake off those January Blues!    Cinnamon Jones presents an electrifying tribute,‘The Lady of Song’, celebrating the legacy of iconic Black female singers.Through soulful renditions and powerful storytelling, she honours the voices of legends like Aretha Franklin, Nina Simone, and Ella Fitzgerald. This performance is a heartfelt journey through music history, showcasing the resilience, artistry, and impact of these trailblazing women.          Bernie Senensky Trio present Jazz in the Spring    Please note:  One of the NJF  JAZZ 4 the AGES youth performers will be the opening act for both performances at The Hare Wine Co..  Artists TBC                          BUY PASSES    ______________________________________________________________________________________________  "
      }
