    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Sunday, March 16th, 2025  🕑TIME: 6:30 pm – 9:00 pm  🏟️VENUE: Mahtay Café &amp; Lounge  🗺️ADDRESS: 241 St. Paul Street, St. Catharines  💵PRICE: $33 + HST + Fees  💵DISCOUNT:  $19 + HST + Fees - MAWS Discount   (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students)   🍕 FOOD: options are available for purchase on site  🚗 PARKING: Free Street Parking                BUY TICKETS                              Presented by the Niagara Jazz Festival in partnership with    Twilight Jazz Series Sponsor                      ABOUT THE SHOW      'Guitar Jazz'  Renowned Canadian jazz guitarist Lorne Lofsky is set to deliver a mesmerizing guitar jazz trio performance, showcasing his signature blend of intricate harmonies, fluid phrasing, and masterful improvisation.  The trio will be performing selections from the Great American Songbook and various Jazz Standards with an open ended, interactive approach.  With a career spanning decades and collaborations with jazz greats like Oscar Peterson, Lofsky’s refined touch and rich tonal palette promise an evening of sophisticated, dynamic jazz, offering jazz enthusiasts an unforgettable musical experience.  Lorne Lofksy on Guitar  Neil Swainson on Bass  Barry Romberg on Drums        ABOUT  LORNE  Lorne Lofsky is an internationally recognized jazz guitarist that’s played/ recorded with a who’s who of Jazz including Oscar Peterson, Ed Bickert and Chet Baker. He played extensively throughout Europe with Mr. Peterson from 1994-96. In addition, he taught at York University for 48 years and has been a mainstay of the music scene for the last several decades in the GTHA, across Canada, and recently in Europe with the Juno nominated Canadian Jazz Collective.    Born, raised, and based in Toronto, Canada, Lofsky’s career began when Oscar Peterson offered to produce his first record, It Could Happen To You (Pablo Records), in 1980. During the years that followed, Lofsky worked extensively in the Toronto area and toured with the likes of Pat LaBarbera, and fellow guitarist Ed Bickert. Bickert and Lofsky’s fruitful collaboration ran from 1983 through 1991 and produced two widely-acclaimed recordings including the well-known 1990 Concord release This Is New.    A master guitarist known for pianistic voicings and virtuosic skill, Lorne Lofsky is considered one of Canada’s great musical treasures. This Song Is New is his first recording as a leader in over two decades and signals an exciting new page in the guitarist’s illustrious career.  ABOUT  THE BAND  Neil Swainson, is a distinguished Canadian jazz bassist. Throughout his career, he has collaborated with notable artists such as Woody Shaw and Joe Henderson, and released his own album, 49th Parallel, in 1987. Swainson also had a long-standing association with pianist George Shearing, performing together from 1988 until Shearing's passing in 2011.    Read more...    Barry Romberg is a prominent Canadian jazz drummer known for his unique style and significant contributions to the jazz scene. Over his extensive career, he has collaborated with renowned artists such as Gil Evans, Joe Henderson, and Sam Rivers, and has been featured on over 70 recordings, including 12 as a leader or co-leader.                      BUY TICKETS  "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "TWILIGHT JAZZ SERIES:  Lorne Lofsky Trio"
      }
