    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATES: Monday, April 7th / Monday, May 5th / Monday, June 2nd  💵 SHOWS: Loralee McGuirl Quartet/ Anthony D'Alessandro Quintet feat. Summer Camargo / John Alcorn Trio  🏟️VENUES: The Hare Wine Co.   🗺️ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake  💵 SERIES PASS: $109 + HST + Fees (Includes 3 shows - does not include food)  🍕 FOOD: Available for purchase  🚗 PARKING: Free on site                    BUY PASSES                            Presented by the Niagara Jazz Festival in partnership with                        ABOUT THE SHOWS  Loralee McGuirl is a Canadian jazz singer known for her rich voice and captivating performances. With a deep understanding of jazz standards, she brings a unique blend of emotional depth and technical skill to her music. McGuirl has performed extensively across Canada, earning a reputation for her dynamic stage presence and ability to connect with audiences.        Anthony D'Alessandro is a talented Canadian jazz pianist, composer, and educator, known for his expressive and versatile playing. His performances blend technical mastery with a deep understanding of jazz traditions, earning him recognition in the Canadian jazz scene. D'Alessandro has performed at prominent festivals and venues, showcasing his ability to engage listeners through both his solo work and collaborations with other jazz artists.    Summer Camargo, a 23-year-old trumpeter from Hollywood, Florida, is a Jerome Greene Fellowship recipient at The Juilliard School, where she earned her bachelor’s and master’s degrees. She is a regular performer at renowned NYC jazz clubs and became the youngest member of the Saturday Night Live house band in 2022. With numerous awards, including the Laurie Frink Grant and Ella Fitzgerald Outstanding Soloist Award, Summer has also released her debut album To Whom I Love in 2024, earning recognition in DownBeat magazine’s &quot;25 for the Future&quot; list.    John Alcorn is a renowned Canadian jazz vocalist, composer, lyricist, and producer, acclaimed for his interpretation of the &quot;great American songbook&quot; and his collaborations with top jazz musicians. His accolades include Jazz Report's Male Vocalist of the Year and a Dora Award for Outstanding Music, with his latest album, Flying Without Wings, featuring an all-star Canadian trio and New York cornetist Warren Vaché.  www.johnalcorn.com/    Please note:  One of the NJF  JAZZ 4 the AGES youth performers will be the opening act for both performances at The Hare Wine Co..  Artists TBC                          BUY PASSES    ___________________________________________________________________________________________  "
      }
    ],
