      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Monday, April 7th, 2025  🕑TIME: 7:00 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake  💵PRICE: $43 + HST + Fees  💵DISCOUNT:  $23 + HST + Fees - MAWS Discount   (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students)   🍕 FOOD: Artisanal Pizzas and other options are available for purchase on site  🚗 PARKING: Free on site                BUY TICKETS                              Presented by the Niagara Jazz Festival in partnership with                      ABOUT THE SHOW        ABOUT LORALEE  Juno Nominated, multi-award winning singer and songwriter, Loralee McGuirl is from Hamilton Ontario. Loralee is known for her versatile vocal styles. Her roots are Celtic based with Gospel and Church music as her foundation, being a pastors kid, music was always around. She played began singing publicly with the McGuirl Girls a the age of 3 and began playing clarinet in an orchestra when she was 7. Her love of music was evident and she began winning vocal awards in Elementary school and at Kiwana fesitvals. In High School, she was involved in as many musicals as possible and her music teacher handed her the baton at age 16 and she was conducting the High School band and choir. Under the direction of Brenda Uchimaru, Vox Neaveux became a spring board for the rest of the music career and provided opportunities to sing with Susan Aglukark at the Canadian Country Music Awards, Michelle Wright, Frank Mills, the Nylons, Stan Rodgers Family and many more Canadian Celebrities.    __________________________________________________    ABOUT THE BAND          Loralee McGuirl on Vocals    Nancy Walker on Piano    Clark Johnston on Bass    Joel Haynes on Drums          ______________________________________________    Opening act:  JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Performer Khloe Kalman    Khloe Kalman was born in Hamilton in 2013. She lives in Brantford and attends Ecole Confederation School. She has always shown an immense interest in singing, and great sense for different genres. At the age of four she was featured with the Brock University Wind Ensemble, and in December 2022 she performed with the Brock University Jazz Ensemble and brought down the house in her appearances.    Her accomplishments include first place at the OMFA Provincial Finals level 1 Classical Voice in 2022, and second place in 2023.    CLICK HERE to read more about Khloe.                                  BUY TICKETS  "
      }
    ],
