    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Monday, June 2nd, 2025  🕑TIME: 7:00 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake  💵PRICE: $43 + HST + Fees  💵DISCOUNT:  $23 + HST + Fees - MAWS Discount   (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students)   🍕 FOOD: Artisanal Pizzas and other options are available for purchase on site  🚗 PARKING: Free on site          BUY TICKETS                              Presented by the Niagara Jazz Festival in partnership with                      ABOUT THE SHOW      John Alcorn expertly interprets the classics of the Great American Songbook, infusing each song with both reverence and originality. Alcorn's ability to connect deeply with the lyrics and convey emotion through his voice makes his performances truly unforgettable.    JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Performer     Info coming soon...    ABOUT JOHN ALCORN      John Alcorn is one of Canada’s premier jazz vocalists, celebrated for his work as a singer, composer, lyricist, arranger, and producer. He has received numerous accolades, including Jazz Report's Male Vocalist of the Year and a Dora Award for Outstanding Music. Known for his vast repertoire and original interpretations, Alcorn has collaborated with top jazz musicians and released the album Flying Without Wings, featuring an all-star Canadian trio and New York cornet player Warren Vaché.    CLICK HERE for more information about John.          ABOUT THE BAND      John Alcorn on Vocals    Brian Dickinson on Piano    Pat Collins on Bass                        BUY TICKETS  "
      }
