    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Saturday, June 14th, 2025  🕑TIME: 11 am – 9 pm*  🏟️VENUE: Various venues*  🗺️ADDRESS: Queen Street Niagara Falls, ON   💵PRICE: FREE to enter but tickets for festival workshops are additional  🍤  FOOD: Available on at our Venue Partners on Queen Street  🍷DRINKS: Available on at our Venue Partners on Queen Street  * See full schedule below  ** Select workshops require payment (see below)              WORKSHOP TICKETS              [table id=52 /]  DOWNLOAD SCHEDULE    ABOUT THE EVENT:  Niagara Jazz Festival presents  Big Easy 2nd Line Celebration  Get ready for New Orleans of the North!   🎺 Strut your stuff along Queen Street alongside the Brass Bands 🎤 Enjoy performances featuring Turbo Street Funk, Dragon Ritual Drummers and more...🍤 Savor the flavors of New Orleans with Cajun &amp; Creole menu features  🍸 Sip and indulge in signature cocktails from the Crescent City  🎭 Dress to impress with feathers, beads, masks, and festive flair!  On Saturday, June 14, 2025, from 11 am - 9 pm, Queen St. in Niagara Falls will burst to life with a vibrant Big Easy 2nd Line Celebration, kicking off the Niagara Jazz Festival's summer season. Inspired by New Orleans traditions, the celebration will feature strolling brass bands, drummers, dancing, activities for all ages, and a joyous crowd celebrating jazz, live music and community spirit.          &nbsp;  What is a Second Line?  The Second Line in New Orleans is a vibrant street parade tradition rooted in African American culture. It features a &quot;main line&quot;, usually a brass band leading the procession. The &quot;second line,&quot; made up of dancing, parasol-twirling participants who follow, celebrating life with music, movement, and community spirit. Often seen at weddings, funerals, and festivals, the Second Line is a powerful symbol of joy, resilience, and cultural pride.        Our partners for this special event include Niagara Falls Innovation Hub; Niagara Falls University Canada, Taps Brewhouse, Cat &amp; Monkey AWA (African Women Acting), No Tell Cocktail and Speakeasy and Steve Wilson Studio. Additionally, Downtown Niagara Falls Queen Street merchants will also join in the revelry by adding their own flair with lively in-store promotions, New Orleans-themed activities, and creative displays that reflect the spirit of the celebration.  From hosting interactive workshops, cocktail and food demos, arts and crafts workshops, special discounts, pop-up performances to themed menus and storefront décor, local businesses will help transform Queen Street into a vibrant, immersive experience for festival goers.  This festive pre-launch event not only previews the main festival Flagship event, Summer Mardi Gras (June 20 @ Oakes Garden Theatre),it also celebrates the rich blend of local culture, music, culinary, and community in downtown Niagara Falls!  Festival goers will feel energized, immersed in a lively, joyful celebration of music, culture, and community, where every corner of Queen Street pulses with the spirit of New Orleans.          &nbsp;  Culinary and Cocktail Features:  Here are some of the specialty Mardi Gras themed items that will be sold at our various venue partners during the event.  &nbsp;  No Tell Cocktail is Offering:  Hurricane Cocktails  Sign up for the Cocktail Making Demo HERE  Learn to craft the iconic Hurricane cocktail in a lively, hands-on demo filled with festive flair. Guests will enjoy their own Hurricane Cocktail they will create.  4:00 pm – 4:30pm, 4:45 pm – 5:15 pm, 5:30 pm – 6:00 pm, 6:15 pm – 6:45 pm, 7:00 pm – 7:30 pm    Gumbo      &nbsp;  Plush Imperial is Offering:      &nbsp;    &nbsp;              Youth Performers:        1. Quibble Quabble Quartet  2. Emilio Geremia  3. Carly Greavette                                        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  TURBO STREET FUNK                      CLICK HERE for more information about Turbo Street Funk    &nbsp;    DRAGON RITUAL DRUMMERS        CLICK HERE for more information about Dragon Ritual Drummers             TRASH PANDA BRASS                  JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Performers        Quibble Quabble Quartet is a sax quartet from the Woodlands Secondary School in Mississauga. Jason Gali, leading the quartet on soprano sax, began piano at 6 and the alto sax at 11. He is passionate about learning about musical composition and mastering jazz improvisation. CLICK HERE for more info.  We also have Emilio Geremia and Carly Greauette performing at the Big Easy 2nd Line Celebration.              WORKSHOP TICKETS                                          Event Funder          Event Partners and Sponsors         &nbsp;                                   &nbsp;    &nbsp;          &nbsp;          &nbsp;              Supported by          Sponsored by            &nbsp;      &nbsp;                    BUY FESTIVAL WEEKEND PASSES                              PLEASE NOTE:      This is an outdoor event, and it will take place Rain or Shine    Tickets for the workshops are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
