    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: June 23rd   🕑TIME: 7:00pm  🏟️VENUE: Cat &amp; Monkey  🗺️ADDRESS: Queen Street Niagara Falls, ON   💵PRICE: $20                  BUY TICKETS            Saint John’s Eve Interactive Ceremony w/ Witchdoctor Utu   Monday, June 23rd - 7:00 pm – 9:00 pm  Cat &amp; Monkey, 4548 Queen Street, Niagara Falls L2E 2L5  FEE: $20 + HST + Fees  *Space is limited and will fill up quickly  Buy Tickets: https://www.showpass.com/saint-johns-eve-celebration/  Join Witchdoctor Utu and members of the Dragon Ritual Drummers at Cat &amp; Monkey in Niagara Falls, for a unique cultural celebration and ceremony to recognize Saint John’s Eve. Saint John’s Eve celebrations all have a slightly different flavour depending on what country and region they take place. In the Creole and Cajun communities Saint John’s Eve is a night for cleansing, empowerment and embracing the many mysteries that Saint John’s Eve represents. Utu and the Dragon Ritual Drummers will share an evening of music, stories and ending with an interactive ceremony to uplift, empower and inspire the attendees for a one-of-a-kind intimate gathering.                    BUY TICKETS                                              Event Funder          Event Partners and Sponsors                           &nbsp;                        Supported by          Sponsored by                       SUMMER FESTIVAL WEEKEND PASSES                              PLEASE NOTE:      This is an outdoor event, and it will take place Rain or Shine    Tickets for the workshops are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "St. John’s Eve Interactive Ceremony"
      }
    ],
