        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Monday, June 9th  🕑TIME: 5:30 pm - 7:00 pm  🏟️VENUE:  University of Niagara Falls Canada  🗺️ADDRESS: 4342 Queen Street  💵PRICE: Ticketed/ Pay What You Can                  GET TICKETS              ABOUT THE EVENT  Snakebite Session: Up Close with The Snake Charmer    Brace yourself for a bold bite of inspiration!    Join us for a thrilling Snakebite Session with the one and only Archy J, The Snake Charmer: India’s first professional female bagpiper, self-taught sensation, and genre-defying artist blending Celtic, Indian, and even metal music into her electrifying sound.    Discover how Archy became a YouTube sensation, with nearly 800,000 subscribers and attracting millions of views with her powerful, one-of-a-kind performances    From the streets of New Delhi to global stages and even a nod from the President of India, Archy’s journey is as fierce as her music.    Hosted by Juliet Dunn, Executive Artistic Producer of the Niagara Jazz Festival, this candid convo dives into Archy's creative evolution, followed by a live audience Q&amp;A.    Come for the story... stay for the spark!This is one Snakebite you’ll actually want to feel!    ---    ABOUT ARCHY J - The Snake Charmer    The Snake Charmer, also known as Archy J, is India’s first professional female bagpiper, recognized by the President of India for her pioneering work. A self-taught musician from New Delhi, she has gained international acclaim for her innovative fusion of traditional bagpipe music with diverse genres, including Celtic, Indian, and even metal. Her unique covers of popular songs, such as “Zombie,” “Star Wars Theme,” and “Pirates of the Caribbean,” have garnered millions of views on YouTube.    In addition to her cover tracks, The Snake Charmer has released original compositions that blend bagpipes with various musical styles. Notably, her 2019 single “Aasman Se (From the Sky)” combines bagpipes with Indian percussion and bilingual vocals, celebrating diversity and inclusivity . Her 2023 release, “Scotland the Brave India the Bold,” further exemplifies her ability to merge cultural elements through music.    Beyond her musical achievements, The Snake Charmer is dedicated to promoting the bagpipe as a versatile instrument capable of transcending cultural boundaries. Through her performances and compositions, she continues to inspire audiences worldwide, demonstrating the power of music to bridge diverse traditions and foster global connections.    ​                    GET TICKETS                                              Event Funder          Official Transportation Sponsor    Event Partners and Sponsors                           &nbsp;                                                     Supported by          Sponsored by                                               PLEASE NOTE:      This is an indoor event    Tickets are non-refundable    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
