    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Monday, December 1st, 2025  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 789 Niagara Stone Road, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $39 + HST + FEES  💵DISCOUNT (MAWSU):  $19 + HST + FEES  (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30)  🍕 FOOD: Snack foods available on site.   🍷DRINKS: Cash bar on site  🚗 PARKING: Free on site     *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm                 BUY TICKETS                    ABOUT THE SHOW        🎶 The Voices of Jazz 🎶  An unforgettable night celebrating the biggest names in vocal jazz! Join acclaimed singer and saxophonist Christopher Plock alongside a lineup of top-tier jazz vocalists for a night of timeless standards, soulful ballads, and swinging duets. From Ella to Sinatra and beyond, this is a show where legends live on — and the music never stops.                ABOUT THE ARTISTS  Christopher Plock Trio - Vocals and Saxophone  Two-time JUNO Award-winning Christopher Plock is Toronto’s versatile singer and saxophonist extraordinaire. Known for his rich voice, multi‑instrumental chops, and unforgettable stage presence, Chris blends standards, jazz, blues, and big‑band flair into a live show that both soothes and energizes. From timeless crooner moments to dance‑floor grooves, he delivers a performance you won’t want to miss.    “A Voice Like Velvet. A Sax That Sizzles.”            Eric St. Laurent - Guitar    Born in Montreal, Eric studied guitar and improvisation in New York City before moving to Berlin, where he spent a decade as a sideman to big and small names of the European music world. After relocating to Toronto, he worked as a studio and live musician and dove into blues, country, and music tech. This interest in art and technology has led to recent recordings exploring common ground between composition, electronica, and various global music traditions.      Mark Dunn - Bass    Mark was born into a musical family and started playing piano at age 3. He began playing saxophone professionally at age 14. He navigated his way through several instruments through the 1970’s before settling on bass in 1980. After finishing college in 1985 he continued his studies with various artists in Montreal, New York, and of course, Toronto. He has performed at numerous jazz festivals in Toronto, Niagara, Eastern Ontario, and toured England and the US at folk and rock festivals. He continues to perform at local clubs and restaurants in the GTA and surrounding areas. He currently holds the bass chair for two of Toronto’s longest working big bands, Martin Loomer’s Orange Devils, and the Jim Galloway Wee Big Band.  Sent from my iPhone                  BUY TICKETS                              Presented by    Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment                     In partnership with          Sponsored by:    Partners:                      BUY TICKETS                            PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
