      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Sunday, December 21st, 2025  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9 pm  🏟️VENUE: SECRET VENUE (TBA)  🗺️ADDRESS:  SECRET VENUE (TBA)  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $33 + HST + FEES  💵DISCOUNT (MAWSU):  $19 + HST + FEES  (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30)   💵PASSES for FULL SERIES: (3 events - Oct 19, Nov 16, Dec 21):   $79 + HST + FEES  🍕 FOOD: Snack foods available on site.   🍷DRINKS: Cash bar on site  🚗 PARKING: Free on site     *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm                 BUY TICKETS            ABOUT THE SHOW        🎶 Mistletoe &amp; Melodies 🎶  Get into the festive spirit with jazz vocalist Juliet Dunn as she shares her favourite holiday classics, backed by Doug Mundy (piano) and Clark Johnston (bass). With warm vocals and swinging solos, it’s the perfect way to kick off your holiday season.  “Holiday warmth, jazz charm.”                  ABOUT THE ARTIST   Juliet Dunn is a Canadian jazz vocalist, producer, and community builder based in Niagara. After spending 13 years in Paris, she returned home where she moved between theatre, radio, and jazz performance. She co-founded the TD Niagara Jazz Festival and the Twilight Jazz Series with her late husband, Peter Shea and is currently the Executive &amp; Artistic Director of the festival and her own company JADE (Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment).  These initiatives have helped cultivate a vibrant jazz community in the Niagara Region of Ontario, Canada, and spotlight both emerging and established talent.   With her charismatic presence and love for storytelling through song, Juliet Dunn continues to enchant audiences and keep the spirit of jazz alive and swinging.          CLICK HERE for more information about Juliet.                      BUY TICKETS                              Presented by    Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment                     In partnership with                        Part of the                BUY TICKETS                            PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
