        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Sunday, December 21st, 2025  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9 pm  🏟️VENUE: SECRET VENUE (TBA)  🗺️ADDRESS:  SECRET VENUE (TBA)  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $33 + HST + FEES  💵DISCOUNT (MAWSU):  $19 + HST + FEES  (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30)   💵PASSES for FULL SERIES: (3 events - Oct 19, Nov 16, Dec 21):   $79 + HST + FEES  🍕 FOOD: Snack foods available on site.   🍷DRINKS: Cash bar on site  🚗 PARKING: Free on site     *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm                 BUY TICKETS        BUY SERIES PASSES                                  ABOUT THE SHOW        🎶 Hidden Gems &amp; Buried Treasures - Discovering the Lost Verses 🎶  Often lost to the mists of time, the vast Great North American Songbook offers hundreds of examples of buried treasures in Verses - those forgotten bits of music that precede the much-loved and well-remembered refrains.          Experience the joy of renewing your love for these great songs as Ross and Carolyn dust off these delicious morsels of music and tell you the history behind each song! Marvel at the beautiful interpretations of Carolyn Credico, and Ross at the piano.    &quot;Unearthing the rarely heard verses&quot;                          ABOUT THE ARTISTS  Born 1962 in Hamilton Ontario, Ross Wooldridge showed early musical ability,taking piano lessons by age four. Inspired by the big band music of Artie Shaw and Benny Goodman, Ross taught himself to play the clarinet at age 13. Later on at 16 he took up the saxophone and the flute. Attending Mohawk College and Humber College, Ross honed his arranging and  composing skills. Afterwards he added to his portfolio the skills of Producer,Conductor, Transcription specialist and Educator.    Ross enjoys co-leading the traditional jazz band the Dixie Demons with trombonist Dan Douglas, and a busy career of playing and recording with his Tribute to the Benny Goodman Sextet, and Tribute to Artie Shaw and his Gramercy 5, and his various big band shows such as Benny Meets Artie – the Hits of Artie Shaw and Benny Goodman. Notable names he has recorded with are Peter Appleyard, Don Thompson, Alex Pangman, Jaymz Bee, Terra  Hazelton and the late Jeff Healey. Leader of The Ross Wooldridge Orchestra and The Galaxy Orchestra, Rosshas written many of their arrangements and produced their CD “Tribute to the  Kings of Swing” which is played regularly on radio stations across North America. Recordings are available from Ross’ website www.rosswooldridge.com. Notable are his critically acclaimed recordings Tribute to the Benny Goodman Sextet Volumes 1 and 2, Scuttlebutt – a Tribute to Artie Shaw and his Gramercy 5 and two Dixie Demons recordings “Live at the Rex” and “Fossil Fuel”. Recently Ross produced and arranged the new album by Brenda Brown “Life  Among Giants”, a dynamic recording featuring a stellar big band and concert  orchestra.  Carolyn Credico Carolyn Credico is a sweet, soulful jazz, R&amp;amp;B, and pop singer from the Hamilton area.  She enrolled in the Applied Music Program at Mohawk College in Hamilton where she studied jazz voice under the guidance of Bob Hamper.  During her time at Mohawk, Carolyn was selected to do a one-hour interview on 91.1 Jazz FM's &quot;Jazzology&quot; program. After graduating in 2011,Carolyn recorded her first full-length jazz album titled &quot;Pieces of Dreams&quot;; with Don Thompson, Reg Schwager and Pat Collins.  She performs in Toronto for some of 91.1 Jazz FM events organized by Jaymz Bee, and sings at local venues and private events throughout the GTA, Hamilton, and Niagara Region.                            BUY TICKETS        BUY SERIES PASSES                                  Presented by    Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment                     In partnership with                        Part of the                BUY TICKETS      BUY SERIES PASSES                              PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
