    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Sunday, December 7th, 2025  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9 pm  🏟️VENUE: The Secret Venue:  The Warehouse Concert Hall  🗺️ADDRESS:  11 Geneva Street, St. Catharines  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $33 + HST + FEES  💵DISCOUNT (MAWSU):  $19 + HST + FEES  (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30)    🍕 FOOD: Snack foods available on site.   🍷DRINKS: Cash bar on site  🚗 PARKING: Free on site     *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm                 BUY TICKETS            ABOUT THE SHOW        🎶 Electric Grooves 🎶  Electric Grooves is a bold, high-energy night of jazz-rock fusion, featuring powerhouse drummer Randolf Jimenez and his band. Blending deep grooves and inspired improvisation, this live set promises a thrilling journey through rhythm, energy, and electrifying sound.    Randolf Jimenez (Drums)  Bureh Bollo-Kamar (Guitar)  Vinnie Venkov (Bass guitar)                  ABOUT THE ARTIST  Randolf Jimenez   Hailed by Billboard Magazine as &quot;one of the best Latin-American drummers nowadays,&quot; Randolf Jimenez is a renowned drummer, composer, and bandleader with over 20 years of experience performing with Grammy and Latin Grammy-winning artists. Since moving to Canada in 2013, he has become known as Toronto’s most sought-after Latin drummer, performing at top venues across the country including Massey Theatre, Queen Elizabeth Theatre, and Glenn Gould Studio. Featured in publications such as All About Jazz, Tokyo Jazz Review, and CARAS Magazine, Randolf now leads the Randolf Jimenez Band—a powerhouse ensemble that fuses jazz sophistication with rock energy to deliver an electrifying live experience. He is also an official endorser of Sonor drums and Paiste cymbals.  CLICK HERE for more information about Randolf.                            BUY TICKETS                              Presented by    Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment                     In partnership with                        Part of the                BUY TICKETS                            PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
