      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Monday, February 2nd, 2026  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 789 Niagara Stone Road, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $39 + HST + FEES  💵DISCOUNT (Promo Code - MAWSU2026): -50% (19.50) + HST + FEES (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30) 🍕 FOOD: Snack foods available on site. 🍷DRINKS: Wine by the glass available 🚗 PARKING: Free on site   $19 + HST + FEES  (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30)  🍕 FOOD: Snack foods available on site.   🍷DRINKS: Wine by the glass available  🚗 PARKING: Free on site     *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm                 BUY TICKETS          BUY a SERIES PASS        ABOUT THE SHOW          🎶 A CELEBRATION OF BLACK MUSICAL LEGACY 🎶      An intimate, musically rich evening that blends jazz, soul, and timeless classics delivered with warmth, refinement, and emotional depth. Through thoughtful interpretation and expressive storytelling, Khea shapes a performance that feels personal, immersive, and deeply present.  In recognition of Black History Month, the evening gently highlights the spirit  and influence of Black musical heritage, threading its depth and history through an  experience that feels both timeless and profoundly connected.                    ABOUT THE ARTISTS      Khea Emmanuel:    Khea, daughter of legendary Motown artist Leroy Emmanuel, is a fearless, self-taught vocalist and songwriter with a deeply rooted love for jazz, blues, R&amp;B, and the classics. Her emotionally charged vocals, heartfelt lyrics, and unforgettable presence captivate audiences of all ages.    Khea has performed alongside and for renowned artists and VIPs, including Natalie Cole, Anne Margaret, Goldie Hawn, and Janice Mitchell, and has appeared at major galas, festivals, and sold-out performances across Canada. She has also developed original music in Los Angeles with the late legendary producer Bob Esty, further shaping her distinctive and soulful sound.    CLICK HERE for Khea's full bio.    Khea will be accompanied by Doug Mundy on Piano and Clark Johnston on Bass.                                BUY TICKETS                BUY a SERIES PASS                Presented by    Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment                     In partnership with          Sponsored by:                    BUY TICKETS                BUY a SERIES PASS                  PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
