    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Sunday, March 22, 2026  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9 pm  🏟️VENUE: SECRET VENUE REVEALED: Aura on the Lake   🗺️ADDRESS: 233 King Street, Niagara-on-the-Lake  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $33 + HST + FEES  💵DISCOUNT (Promo Code - MAWSU-2026):  - 50% ($16.50) + HST + FEES  (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30)  💵SERIES PASS PRICE (3 Shows: Feb 15 / Mar 8/Mar 22): $79 + HST + FEES  🍕 FOOD: Food - CLICK HERE for Menu*  * If you plan on dining be sure to reserve in advance - CALL:  905.468.7222  🍷DRINKS: Wine by the glass and bottle / Beer / Non-alcoholic options   🚗 PARKING: Street parking     *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm   * If you plan on dining be sure to reserve in advance - CALL: 905.468.7222               ABOUT JULIET DUNN'S SECRET SALON SERIES         Experience live music like never before. Curated by vocalist and producer and Niagara Jazz Festival co-creator and Executive and Artistic Director, Juliet Dunn, the Secret Salon Series brings intimate performances to unique, undisclosed venues across Niagara — revealed only days before the show.  Expect world-class musicians, cozy vibes, and unforgettable nights of jazz, soul, and discovery.  Limited tickets. Secret location. Pure magic!   Where music meets mystery.                BUY TICKETS            ABOUT THE SHOW          🎶 SHADOWS &amp; LIGHTS 🎶      An intimate evening of voice and piano, this performance invites listeners into the quiet heart of Whitney Ross-Barris's latest release, Curtains of Light. Rooted in jazz yet fearlessly genre-bending, the music unfolds with threads of soul, spoken word, classical, folk, and choral influences. Stripped down to its essence, each song is given space to breathe—lyrics come into sharp focus, melodies linger, and the emotional core of the record shines through. This is a close, reflective listening experience where nuance, storytelling, and connection take center stage.        &nbsp;                ABOUT THE ARTISTS      Whitney Ross-Barris is an Ontario-based jazz singer, pianist, and songwriter with proud roots in the theatre. With a velvet voice and a sharp wit, her songs as well as her live performances are an inviting and unexpectedly immersive experience of off-the-cuff story-telling and exciting musicianship.    Adrean Farrugia is a Canadian award-winning jazz pianist, composer, and educator known for his expressive style and wide-ranging collaborations. He has toured internationally, appeared on 60+ recordings, and earned multiple Juno Awards and nominations. Farrugia is also a respected teacher, having taught at several Canadian universities, and continues to shape the jazz scene as both a performer and mentor.    &nbsp;                                BUY TICKETS                              Presented by    Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment                     In partnership with          Sponsored by:                        BUY TICKETS                                PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
