    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Friday, February 20th, 2026  🕑TIME: 6 pm – 10 pm (Concert starts at 7 pm)  🏟️VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Road, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON   💵PRICE: $39+ HST Table seating) / $19 = HST (theatre-style seating)  🍕 FOOD: Various menu options available - Menu options coming shortly  🍷DRINKS: Wine by the glass available + non-alcoholic options  🚗 PARKING: Free on site    *Dinner from 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm     PLEASE NOTE:    This is a 'show only' ticket. Food is available on site for an additional cost. Food options (including select items from JamRock Irie Jerk) will be posted and emailed to all ticket holders shortly. Also on our social media channels:  @jazzniagara    Ticket options:    $39 + HST for guests who require a table and will be ordering food.  $19 + HST for guests who will be having drinks only. Theatre-style seating (close to the stage) is available.              BUY TICKETS            ABOUT THE SHOW          🎶 BLACK HISTORY, BOLD FLAVOURS, TIMELESS MUSIC.🎶      Get ready for an exclusive music experience at one of the best wineries in Niagara!  Join us for an unforgettable night featuring a live performance by Velvet Frequencies —in Niagara's favourite 'Jazz Club'.  The Niagara Jazz Festival and Hare Wine Co. present an intimate evening of soulful sounds and timeless vibes in a stunning Niagara-on-the-Lake winery.  In honour of Black History Month, this special performance celebrates the profound legacy and lasting influence of Black artists who shaped the sound of jazz, soul, and contemporary music. From the spiritual roots and resilience that gave birth to these genres to the bold innovation of today’s creators, the evening traces a powerful musical lineage across generations.  Rooted in soul, rhythm, and creative freedom, the experience blends classic influences with fresh, original sounds—bringing past, present, and future frequencies together in perfect harmony while honouring Black excellence, artistry, and cultural impact.                  BUY TICKETS                    ABOUT THE ARTISTS      Featuring Tone - Vocals    Hailing from Niagara Falls, Ontario, Tone is a neo-soul artist whose music is rooted in authenticity, reflection, and upliftment. Blending smooth soul textures with heartfelt lyrics, Tone creates soundscapes that inspire growth, resilience, and self-belief. Drawing directly from lived experience, his music tells honest stories of struggle, healing, and triumph, offering listeners both comfort and motivation.    With a deep respect for soul traditions and a modern creative edge, Tone’s artistry bridges the past and present—delivering music that feels timeless yet personal. Each song is an invitation to slow down, feel deeply, and reconnect with purpose. Whether through intimate melodies or empowering messages, Tone’s mission remains clear: to use music as a force for inspiration, healing, and positive energy.                Brent Setterington - Keys / Arrangements  Brent Setterington has played the local Niagara scene extensively, debuting with the Jazz Combo he co-created with Peter Shea in their high school days. He has been gigging professionally ever since. As one of the original keyboardists in Niagara’s beloved LMT CONNECTION, Brent cut his teeth on old jazz and funk soul records from the Motown era.  As co-writer, arranger, keyboardist, and musical director of the funk-soul outfit Jacksoul, Brent and Haydain Neale created a unique sound that landed them a major recording contract with BMG in 1995.  CLICK HERE to read full bio                  Special guest:  Leroy Emmanuel - Guitar  Leroy Emmanuel is a Detroit-born guitarist, singer, and songwriter known for his deep roots in soul, R&amp;B, funk, and blues. He began his professional music career as a young teenager, earning early work in Detroit’s vibrant music scene and performing and recording with legendary artists such as Marvin Gaye, Stevie Wonder, Gladys Knight &amp; the Pips, ZZ Hill, and others during the Motown and soul era. Emmanuel was an original member of The Counts and also became a featured player with noted funk artist Hamilton Bohannon, appearing on numerous albums.  In 1989 he co-founded the Canadian funk-soul trio LMT Connection (based in Niagara, Ontario), where he serves as guitarist and lead vocalist. The band blends R&amp;B, jazz, and funk into what they call “Universal Soul” and has recorded multiple albums and toured extensively in North America and Europe. Emmanuel’s guitar style fuses jazz sensibilities with hard funk and soulful expression, and he has been an active performer and teacher for over four decades.                          Joe Cool - Bass        Joseph Barrow (AKA Joe Cool) is a Niagara-based bassist who relocated from the Motor City. A proud member of the Detroit Bass Players, he has been performing since 1977, playing in school jazz ensembles as well as blues, church, pop, funk, and jazz bands. His experience also includes performing in Germany with the U.S. Army Band and U.S. Army Choir.  Joe currently performs with Hausquake and Mel Monaco in the Niagara Region. Known for his deep-in-the-pocket funk, he locks into the groove with dynamic slap bass and melodic rhythmic flair—bringing an irresistible pulse that keeps audiences moving and grooving.                      Marcus Gazzellone - Drums                                 A seasoned drummer with over 25 years of experience, performing with multiple bands across a wide range of genres. Known for a solid pocket, versatility, and bringing energy and precision to every performance. Equally comfortable on stage and in the studio, with a strong focus on timing, dynamics, and serving the song. Marcus is also a songwriter and producer, currently working on his own EP. From tight grooves to high-energy sets, he brings consistency, feel, and a deep passion for music to every project.                        BUY TICKETS                                                                          Presented by                            Sponsored by and in partnership with                  Thanks to our Angel Sponsors:                               BUY TICKETS                                PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email us at guests@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
