    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Thursday, April 30, 2026  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️VENUE: FirstOntario Performing Arts Centre  🗺️ADDRESS: 250 St. Paul, Street, St. Catharines  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $49 + HST + FEES   🍷DRINKS: Wine, Beer &amp; non-alcoholic options available on site  🚗 PARKING: Street parking + Parking lot    *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm                Celebrating  INTERNATIONAL JAZZ DAY with JILL BARBER!         Celebrated worldwide on April 30, International Jazz Day highlights the power of jazz to unite people and cultures through music. Founded by Herbie Hancock and recognized by UNESCO, the day celebrates jazz as a universal language that promotes peace, dialogue, and creativity. 🎷                CLICK HERE to BUY TICKETS             ABOUT THE SHOW  Celebrating International Jazz Day!  To mark the occasion, the Niagara Jazz Festival proudly presents a special vocal jazz concert, in partnership with the FirstOntario Performing Arts Centre,  featuring one of Canada’s finest jazz vocalists, Jill Barber. Renowned for her velvety voice, timeless elegance, and captivating stage presence, Jill brings world-class Canadian jazz artistry to this celebration of the music’s global spirit. 🎶                      ABOUT THE ARTIST      Jill Barber is a three-time Juno-nominated singer-songwriter known for her unforgettable voice and genre-spanning music, from folk and jazz to pop in both English and French. She’ll perform an intimate concert on Thursday, April 30 at 7pm, in the Recital Hall, presented with the Niagara Jazz Festival and FirstOntario Performing Arts Centre—tickets are limited.                Following her 2018 album Metaphora (featuring the #1 hit “Girl’s Gotta Do”), her jazz album Chances achieved Gold status in Canada. She has won major awards, including SiriusXM Jazz Artist of the Year, and earned praise from artists like Kris Kristofferson.  Her music has appeared in shows like Orange Is the New Black, The L Word, and Heartland, and in a global Chrysler campaign. A captivating live performer, she has headlined top venues worldwide, including Massey Hall and the National Arts Centre.                                                Presented by                    In partnership with:                          CLICK HERE to BUY TICKETS                                 PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Pauline at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Celebrating International Jazz Day - JILL BARBER"
      }
    ],
