    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/HB-457x572-1.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/vocal-master-class-with-heather-bambrick/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/artists/heather-bambrick/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Wednesday, June 21, 2023  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 8:30 pm   🏟️ VENUE: Ridley College  🗺️ ADDRESS:  2 Ridley Rd, St. Catharines, ON  💵 PRICE: FREE for students / Pay what you can or for others  * ALL are welcome (not just musicians)        SIGN UP / BUY TICKETS                              ABOUT THE EVENT:  &quot;So, You Wanna Be A Jazz Singer ... &quot;    Join JUNO-nominated vocalist and award-winning JAZZ.FM91 broadcaster Heather Bambrick as she looks at a few of the elements involved in jazz vocal performance and preparation, from stylistic appropriateness to taking a song off the page and making it yours. (Anyone wanting to get some additional pointers can bring along their favorite standard for a brief masterclass-style session as well, as time allows.) Joining Heather for this session will be one of the finest pianists in Canada, the wonderful John Sherwood.    For musicians and those interested in learning an instrument, the TD Niagara Jazz Festival offers Master Classes led by high-caliber jazz artists from Canada and the global stage. These Master Classes offer an unparalleled learning experience for all musicians, and for those who are just beginning their journey into the world of jazz music.        ABOUT THE ARTIST:  Heather Bambrick is a JUNO-nominated vocalist, a voice actor, and an award-winning broadcaster. She’s worked with numerous artists, including Fred Hersch, Guido Basso, Rob McConnell, Ann Hampton Callaway, Peter Appleyard, Lea Delaria, Gene Denovi, Ian Shaw, Jackie Richardson, Phil Nimmons, David Braid, the Caliban Quartet, the Windsor Symphony Orchestra, and many others.    She’s a founding member of both the Beehive Singers and Broadsway, and has released three solo CDs, including her latest “You’ll Never Know”, which was nominated for Vocal Jazz Recording of the Year at the 2017 JUNO Awards.    Learn more about Heather Bambrick        PLEASE NOTE:      Physical/digital tickets are not issued for this event. Admission is tracked through the order placed and will be added to the event’s guest list. Please retain your Order Confirmation email in case proof of purchase is required.    Tickets are non-refundable.    Artists and venues are subject to change.    Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          &nbsp;  HOSTED BY FESTIVAL PARTNER RIDLEY COLLEGE    WITH SUPPORT FROM THE CITY OF ST. CATHARINES        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          SIGN UP / BUY TICKETS  &nbsp;  Supported in part by:  "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Vocal MASTER CLASS with Heather Bambrick"
      }
    ],
