    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Thursday, December 23, 2021  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm - 9:30 pm (Doors open at 6:00 pm)  🏟️ VENUE: Spirit in Niagara Distillery (VACCINATION POLICY IN EFFECT)  🗺️ ADDRESS: 458 Lakeshore Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵 PRICE: Show Only: $49 + HST; Dinner and Show: $119 + HST; Musicians/Arts Workers/Students (Show Only): $23 + HST; Prices include Gratuities - Buy Now!  🎟️ SEASON PASS: 6 shows (NO Charlie Brown seating): $169 + HST; All 7 shows (includes Charlie Brown but NO dinner): $199 + HST; All 7 shows (includes Charlie Brown WITH dinner): $279 + HST - Buy Now!    BUY TICKETSBUY SEASON PASSARTISTSMENUABOUT THE SERIES  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE SHOW  The Music of a Charlie Brown Christmas takes audiences on a nostalgic journey of one of the most beloved holiday albums, created by Vince Guaraldi for the 1965 TV special of the same name. Performed by world-class jazz musicians, this show takes the best of jazz, serves it up with traditional holiday music, and provides a wonderful tradition that will delight the entire family.    The evening's performance will feature:    Opening Performance:      Kai Oszlai on Piano    Main Performance:      Doug Mundy on piano    Tyler Wagler on bass    Adam Bowman on drums    Upon purchase of tickets, please contact Darlene with your party's menu selections &amp; allergies (DINNER AND SHOW ONLY) to admin@niagarajazzfestival.com or call at 289-259-4997.    Season Pass holders must contact Darlene before the show's date to reserve their seating.     Tickets are non-refundable.    VACCINATION POLICY    All musicians, staff, volunteers and patrons at TD Niagara Jazz Festival events must be double-vaccinated.  Proof of vaccination will be required upon arrival    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.    &nbsp;        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  DOUG MUNDY      Doug Mundy, a long time Niagara resident, began studying piano at 10 years of age concentrating on Royal Conservatory of Music repertoire. At age 14, Doug began experimenting with improvisation, mainly playing around with simple blues progressions and pop/rock solos. By age 16, Doug was already performing in rock, blues and country ensembles around the Niagara and Hamilton Regions.    Blues improvisation led to the formal study of music (and history) at Mohawk College, York University and Brock University. Doug has studied jazz harmony, arranging, form and analysis and counterpoint. At York University, Doug had the privilege of studying with Canadian jazz great Don Thompson as well as seminars with Dr. Oscar Peterson.    Doug is currently one of the most in demand musicians in the Niagara area. He is active accompanying vocalists, leading his duo and trio, working as a sideman on gigs and in the studio, as well as performing solo piano at various functions. Doug has recently completed a tour of New Zealand working with a collection of the country’s finest Jazz musicians.    &nbsp;    &nbsp;  Hosted by Spirit in Niagara Distillery          &nbsp;        MENU  Dinner and Show Tickets Only  Appetizer (Choose One)  Caesar Wedge Salad with Crispy Pork Belly  Leek and Potato Soup    Main  Cornish Hen stuffed with Christmas Stuffing and Red Wine Cranberry Sauce  Served with a side of Maple Roasted Roots and Winter Vegetables (one per table)  Vegetarian Option: Gourmet Mac &amp; Cheese with Niagara Gold Cheese and Mustard    Dessert  Chocolate Mousse with Wild Berries Sauce      &nbsp;        Supported In Part By:  "
      }
    ],
