    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Friday, September 3, 2021  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 9:30 pm (Doors open at 6:00 pm)  🏟️ VENUE: Secret location in St. Catharines, North End  💵 PRICE: General Admission: $99; Tent Seating (6 seats): $529 &amp; $559 (plus HST on all prices) - The performance will proceed rain or shine. Tickets are non-refundable.    TICKETS ARE SOLD OUT; CHECK OUT OUR ONLINE EDITION FOR MORE OPTIONS  ONLINE EDITIONSEE MENU  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE SHOW  Live in-person music is returning to the backyard!    Join us on Friday, September 3rd for our VIP-exclusive Dinner and Show, featuring the talent of the Adrean Farrugia Trio, featuring Adrean Farrugia on piano, Jon Maharaj on bass, and Ernesto Cervini on drums! Enjoy this performance with a three-course menu (included in the ticket price), courtesy of Giganti Events and Catering.    Tickets are $99 + HST, and are available in limited quantities. Bringing the entire household with you? Enjoy an entire tent for you and your group (up to 6) for $529 and $559. Add 1-2 seats for an additional fee. The performance will proceed rain or shine. Tickets are non-refundable.    This performance is supported by TD Bank, JAZZAMCO, DJB, Michael Sommer, Winemaker's Vintage, Desjardins, Anchor Pointe, and Stamford Estates.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.        MENU    Appetizer (Choose One)  Pastry Wrapped Brie with Sun-dried Apricots  Grilled Calamari    Main (Choose One)  Filet of Salmon with Bacon Veg Bundle and Roasted Potatoes  Prosciutto and Mozzarella-Stuffed Chicken Breast with Bacon Veg Bundle and Roasted Potatoes  Vegetarian Option: Eggplant Parmigiana    Dessert  Cheesecake with Fresh Raspberry Sauce            ABOUT THE ARTIST: ADREAN FARRUGIA      Adrean Farrugia began playing piano at the age of 12. By age 16 he decided that he would dedicate his life to music. Since then he has become recognized as one of Canada's finest pianists and composers, having shared the music he loves globally with audiences across Canada, the United States, London UK, Paris, Tokyo, TelAviv, Australia, Poland and The Netherlands with artists such as Ernie Watts, Sheila Jordan, Brad Goode, Joel Frahm, Ernesto Cervini, Matt Dusk and The Worst Pop Band Ever.    Adrean serves on the faculties of Mohawk College and Humber College and has conducted masterclasses and workshops for students at the University of Colorado at Boulder, the Sydney Conservatorium, the Polish Jazz Society Summer Workshop, and the University of Toronto. Adrean has played on more than 40 albums to date garnering 4 Juno award nominations, 1 Juno award and 1 Grammy shortlist recognition."
      }
    ],
