    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Saturday, September 4, 2021  🕑 TIME: 7:30 pm – 9:00 pm  🏟️ VENUE: Online  💵 PRICE: Pay What You Can  BUY TICKETS  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          ABOUT THE SHOW  Join us on Saturday, September 4th for the VIRTUAL return to the backyard, featuring the talent of the Adrean Farrugia Trio, featuring Adrean Farrugia on piano, Jon Maharaj on bass, and Ernesto Cervini on drums!    This is a ticketed livestreamed event beginning at 7:30 PM. Tickets for this virtual show are Pay What You Can, with the proceeds supporting our nonprofit organization's efforts to continue bringing music to Niagara and beyond!    This performance is supported by TD Bank, JAZZAMCO, DJB, Michael Sommer, Winemaker's Vintage, Desjardins, Anchor Pointe, and Stamford Estates.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.  ABOUT THE ARTIST: ADREAN FARRUGIA      Adrean Farrugia began playing piano at the age of 12. By age 16 he decided that he would dedicate his life to music. Since then he has become recognized as one of Canada's finest pianists and composers, having shared the music he loves globally with audiences across Canada, the United States, London UK, Paris, Tokyo, TelAviv, Australia, Poland and The Netherlands with artists such as Ernie Watts, Sheila Jordan, Brad Goode, Joel Frahm, Ernesto Cervini, Matt Dusk and The Worst Pop Band Ever.    Adrean serves on the faculties of Mohawk College and Humber College and has conducted masterclasses and workshops for students at the University of Colorado at Boulder, the Sydney Conservatorium, the Polish Jazz Society Summer Workshop, and the University of Toronto. Adrean has played on more than 40 albums to date garnering 4 Juno award nominations, 1 Juno award and 1 Grammy shortlist recognition."
      }
    ],
