    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Live Learn Jazz Series: &quot;Women of the Hour&quot; Part 5 - SAX in the VINEYARD  FEATURING: ALISON YOUNG QUINTET      Date:  Thursday, July 4, 2019  Time:  7 pm – 9:30 pm  Venue:  Stratus Vineyards  Address: 2059 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake  Website: www.stratuswines.com  Price:  $59 (Regular) / $29 (Students, musicians, Arts workers)    *All prices subject to HST and Handling Fees.    Looking for accommodations? CLICK HERE    The LIVE LEARN JAZZ Series was conceived by the TD Niagara Jazz Festival for those patrons who are interested in learning more about jazz music in a fun atmosphere and in a picturesque Niagara setting.  (Local wineries, breweries, distilleries, and parks.)    And this year our theme is: Women of the Hour!    Enjoy the smooth sounds of saxophone (with a full jazz quintet) in the beautiful setting of Stratus Vineyards.    TICKET PRICE: $59 (Regular price) / $29  (Musicians/Students/Arts workers)        - All pricing is subject to HST and handling fees  - Price includes complimentary pour of Stratus wines and hors d'oeuvres  -  This show is PART FIVE of a SIX part series.  CLICK HERE for information on the whole series.     The festival would like to thank Brock University for sponsoring this event.        CLICK HERE to purchase a LIVE LEARN JAZZ Series PASS  ABOUT ALISON  Born and raised in Ottawa, saxophonist and composer Alison Young discovered jazz at an early age, gravitating towards the exuberance and melodicism of Sonny Rollins and Cannonball Adderley, who continue to influence her to this day. As well as being featured in the National Youth Jazz Ensemble at the Ottawa jazz festival in 2001 and 2002, she began playing professionally as a teenager, developing an affinity for soul and R&amp;B as well as jazz. Since moving to Toronto in the early 2000s to study music at the University of Toronto, Alison has been an active presence on the jazz scene, performing regularly in venues such as The Rex, The Jazz Bistro and The Reservoir Lounge, among others, with a variety of projects.    CLICK HERE for Alison's full bio.  Looking to Book a Hotel?  The TD Niagara Jazz Festival is providing you with hotels and Airbnbs at the lowest prices available online. Book your stay directly through the map below! For your convenience, our hotel partner, White Oaks Resort and Spa, is highlighted in green.    NOTE: If the hotel your looking for does not have vacancy for your selected dates, it will not show up on the map.         document.addEventListener(&quot;DOMContentLoaded&quot;, function(e) {      // 1. Edit widget size      var settings22 = {        width: '100%', // set the width in px or %        height: '460px' // set the height in px or %      };      // 2. Fill out your config here and the rest should work      var s22obj = {        aid: 'niagarajazzfestival', // your affiliate id for tracking        address: '2059 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON' , // Lat/Lng or full street address. For latlng use the &quot;lat&quot;:,&quot;lng&quot;: keys instead        checkin: '2019-07-04', //        maincolor: 'FFFFFF', // your main brand color in hex (without the #)        fontcolor: '50B948', // The navbar's font color in hex (without the #)        featuredhcids: '1109445', // Comma seperated list of HotelsCombined IDs to stand out from other hotels          chpincolor: '50b948', // If you have custom hotels, in hex (without the #)        navimage: 'https://niagarajazzfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/NJF-2018-logo.png', // If set, provide an absolute full URL to change the main logo in the navbar (button on the far left) image        markerimage: 'https://niagarajazzfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/NJF-2018-logo.png', // If set, provide an absolute full URL to change the marker (main map pin) image         zoom: '11',         disableautohover: true      };      // Leave this part intact      var params22=''; for (var key in s22obj){if (params22){params22 +='&amp;';}params22 +=key + '=' + encodeURIComponent(s22obj[key]);}var div22=document.getElementById('stay22-script'); div22.insertAdjacentHTML('afterend', '');    });  "
      }
    ],
