    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Monday, July 18, 2022  🕑 TIME: 7:30 pm – 10:30 pm  🏟️ VENUE: Spirit in Niagara Distillery  🗺️ ADDRESS: 458 Lakeshore Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵 PRICE: $19 + HST; Musicians/Arts Workers/Students SAVE 25% with Promo Code: SOSMAWS2022 - Buy Now!       BUY TICKETSBUY SERIES PASSARTISTSABOUT THE SERIESHEALTH AND SAFETYVISIT SPIRIT IN NIAGARA  &nbsp;        ABOUT THE SHOW  The evening's performance will feature the Brenon Parmar Trio.      Brenon Parmar on Alto Saxophone    Tickets: Physical / digital tickets are not issued for this show. Admission is tracked through the order placed, and will be added to the event's guest list. Please retain your Order Confirmation email in case proof of purchase is required.    Tickets are non-refundable. Artists and venues are subject to change.    Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.    &nbsp;        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  BRENON PARMAR      Alto Saxophonist Brenon Parmar (b.2000) is an upcoming performer in the Toronto jazz scene. Currently studying Jazz Performance at the University of Toronto he has been awarded the Mary Alive Stuart Jazz Scholarship, Richard Iorweth Thorman Jazz Scholarship and has had the chance to develop under Kelly Jefferson, John Johnson, John Macleod, and Gordon Foote. Brenon has received multiple awards including the 2015 Best Soloist Award in the Festivals of Music competition (NYC), the Don Strathdee musical excellence award in 2014,  2015, 2017 and a scholarship award to attend the Berklee Five Week program in 2018.    Aside from saxophone Brenon has received a stellar musical education completing his Grade 10 RCM exams in classical piano. He is extremely excited to have the opportunity to play in the TD Niagara Jazz 4 The Ages Youth Competition.    HOSTED BY SPIRIT IN NIAGARA DISTILLERY        &nbsp;        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!"
      }
    ],
