    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Friday, October 26, 2018  🕑 TIME: 6:30 PM - 10:00 PM  🏟️ VENUE: Niagara-on-the-Lake Community Centre (14 Anderson Lane, Niagara-on-the-Lake ON)  💵 PRICE:  $75 + HST *  / $500 + HST * for a table of 8 – Tables are SOLD OUT!    Click HERE to be on the waiting list for this event. The TD NJF team will let you know if there are tickets available by Wednesday, Oct 24th.    * Handling fee applies  To donate and help support the festival:    * Please note that donations accepted to help the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!        ABOUT THE SHOW  Join us for our 3rd annual JAZZ BIG BAND FUNDRAISER featuring Canada’s Sweetheart of Swing:  ALEX PANGMAN, accompanied by  The JIMMY STAHL BIG BAND with guest vocalists JULIET DUNN and PETER SHEA  (See bios below)    Live jazz, dancing, free swing dance lesson with Niagara Lindy Hop, silent and live auction items, door prizes, cash bar and more!  Sweet and Savoury tapas included provided by ‘The Heat is On‘ catering. (see menu below)    CLICK HERE for info on our ONLINE auction items.             * This year 50% of the event proceeds will support Terry Hardy’s efforts of an Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis program at the St.Catharines General Hospital. (CLICK HERE for details)  The rest of the event proceeds go towards producing the 6th annual Not-For-Profit TD Niagara Jazz Festival’s FREE community events.    ALEX PANGMAN's BIO:     Although Alex Pangman grew up a couple of generations late to have sung with Teddy Wilson, the vibrant young vocalist is proud to be known as Canada's Sweetheart of Swing. With pipes aplenty, Juno nominee Pangman possesses the requisite taste, talent and the historical knowledge of an avid record collector to breathe new life into the sturdy standards of the classic jazz era.    A superb song stylist with growing compositional chops, the gifted Toronto scene maker has built a loyal fanbase amongst jazz listeners and dancers alike through her critically acclaimed work with her stacked Alleycats in the studio, nightclubs and concert halls across Canada including three stellar showcases at the Montreal International Jazz Festival. (Her Alleycats band includes Peter Hill on piano, Glenn Anderson on drums, Chris Banks on bass, and John Macleod &amp; Brigham Phillips on cornet/trumpet, Ross Wooldridge on clarinet &amp; sax, and/or Drew Jurecka on violin and reeds, with Jesse Barksdale on guitar.)    For this special fundraiser Alex has kindly agreed to perform with the Jimmy Stahl Big Band!  We're sure you will enjoy the show!    www.alexpangman.com    The JIMMY STAHL BIG BAND BIO:    Founded in 1977, The Jimmy Stahl Big Band has headlined tours while performing extensively throughout Ontario, New York, Michigan, Pennsylvania and Ohio.    Beginning as a gospel big band with “Swingin’ in the Pews”, the band has recently added two more showcases-“American Songbook” and “Sounds of Sinatra”.    The JSB have had the honour of collaborating with a variety of Grammy Award and Dove Award-winning artists such as Ralph Carmichael, Dave Boyer, Phil Driscoll, Ron Kenoly, and Kathy Troccoli. Some of these collaborations were in-studio recordings, while others were live tapings of television specials that aired on NBC, TNN, Global and CTS television networks. Individually as sidemen, band members have worked with legends Doc Severinsen, Tom Jones, Debbie Boone, Pat Boone, Vic Damone, The Yellow Jackets, and Ray Charles to name just a few.    Audiences everywhere have fallen in love with the Jimmy Stahl Big Band, and we trust you will as well!    CLICK HERE for JULIET DUNN's BIO    CLICK HERE for PETER SHEA's BIO    &nbsp;  MENU - Provided by the HEAT is ON Catering      Bread and dip samplers (on each table)    Pulled Pork with Arugula slaw Slider Station    Greek Salad Station    Passed items hot and cold    Caprese skewers with Balsamic drizzle    Vegetable spring roll thai sauce    Assorted Sushi with wasabi pickled ginger and soy    Arancini with spicy tomato sauce    Mini Chipotle Chicken Kabobs    Herbed Mini Quiche    Balsamic Glazed Figs with Brie Chese    Assorted Pastries Table    _________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________    DANCERS, VOLUNTEERS and STAFF:    Your dinner fee is only $25 and we will have a designated area for you to dine.  Purchase it in advance here.        SORRY...  SOLD OUT!    _______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________  Why we would like to donate 50% of the proceeds to the Idiopathic Pulmonary Fibrosis program: CLICK HERE  &nbsp;    &nbsp;  THANK YOU TO OUR 2018 BIG BAND SPONSORS!  Alex Pangman / Band sponsor - Medigas     Coffee and Dessert sponsor - LBW Law Firm     Marketing sponsor - ProResp     Dance sponsor - SullvanPlan     Coat check sponsor - Greenscapes     &nbsp;    Donations and 'in kind' sponsors:    Framing sponsor - MiKreations     Floral sponsor - Regal Florists     Step and Repeat sponsor - Niagara Institute of Music and Arts     &nbsp;    Event co-sponsor - Shea D Duo (Peter Shea and Juliet Dunn)     &nbsp;    Event co-sponsor - JADE      The Heat is on Catering     Chef Mike     &nbsp;    NiagaraLindy Hop     Corks WineBar and Eatery    Willow Cakes and Pastries     The Bagel Oven     CLICK HERE for LIVE AUCTION details and sponsors    #LiveLoveJazz             "
      }
    ],
