    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/Vibes-In-The-Vines-457-x-572.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/vibes-in-the-vines-2023/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/artists/lesley-mitchell-clarke/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Friday, July 21, 2023  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 9:30 pm   (Doors open 1 hour before showtime)  🏟️ VENUE: Henry of Pelham Estate Winery  🗺️ ADDRESS: 1469 Pelham Rd, St. Catharines, ON  💵 PRICE: $59 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE: $29 + HST + Fees   (MAWS Discount: Musician/ArtsWorker/Student - must show proof)  💵 PRICE: 2-Day Pass (July 20 + 21): $89 + HST + Fees  🥗 FOOD:  Patio Dining @ Short Hills Kitchen featuring Chef Erik Peacock (FULL MENU HERE)        BUY SUMMER PASSBUY 2-DAYBUY TICKETSBUY FOODVIEW ALL SHOWS                              ABOUT THE SHOW:  International Jazz artist David Friedman (Berlin) teams up with some of Canada's finest jazz musicians to bring you a memorable evening in the incredible setting of the Henry of Pelham Estate Winery vineyard. Vibes and good vibes in the vines!        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  David Friedman, known for both a dazzling 4-mallet vibraphone technique and profound creativity is regarded as one of the greatest vibraphonists of his generation and remains at the forefront of jazz as both a performer and educator. Born in New York, but based in Berlin for over 30 years, David Friedman has been an esteemed and sought-after member of the European jazz scene for decades. Before moving to Berlin, he was at the center of New York's jazz and recording scene: after a 2-year stint in singer Tim Buckley's band, he appeared on a slew of recordings on CTI and other labels throughout the 1970s and '80s.    David Friedman has performed or recorded with Wayne Shorter, Horace Silver, Hubert Laws, Horacee Arnold, Joe Henderson, Johnny Griffin, Jane Ira Bloom, Ron Carter, Daniel Humair, and John Scofield among other notable artists.    Downbeat magazine voted his Shades of Change as &quot;One of the Year's Best 20 CDs&quot; His acclaimed recording with Chet Baker, Peace  with bassist Buster Williams and drummer Joe Chambers, features five David Friedman compositions.    With vibraphonist Dave Samuels, he co-led the ground-breaking mallet duo, Double Image Their decades-long influence on mallet percussion performances was recognized when, in 2015, they were inducted into the Percussive Arts Society Hall of Fame.    www.david-friedman.de    David will be joined by:      Lorne Lofsky on Guitar    Neil Swainson on Bass    Terry Clarke on Drums    OPENING ACT  Nicholas Speck on Piano and Jakob Durst on Sax will each be opening for this event.  Nicholas Speck was the winner in the Ages 15-17 (Solo Piano) category, and Jakob Durst was the winner in the Ages 16-19 (Solo Sax) category in our 2023 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Competition.    Nicholas Speck Bio HERE    Jakob Durst Bio HERE  EMCEE  This event is Emceed by musician and TD NJF Artistic Consultant Lesley Mitchell-Clarke. BIO HERE        PLEASE NOTE:      Physical/digital tickets are not issued for this show. Admission is tracked through the order placed and will be added to the event’s guest list. Please retain your Order Confirmation email in case proof of purchase is require.    Tickets are non-refundable. Artists and venues are subject to change. Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    Artists and venues subject to change.    This event will take place rain or shine.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          HOSTED BY HENRY OF PELHAM        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETSVIEW ALL SHOWS  &nbsp;  Supported in part by:  Stage Sponsor  "
      }
    ],
