        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Thursday, July 20, 2023  🕑 TIME: 7:00 pm – 10:00 pm   (Doors open 1 hour before showtime)  🏟️ VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ ADDRESS: 769 Niagara Stone Rd, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵 PRICE: $49 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE: $29 + HST + Fees (MAWS Discount:Musician/ArtsWorker/Student - must show proof)  💵 PRICE: Summer Festival Full Pass: $269 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE: Weekend Pass (July 15 + 16): $139 + HST + Fees  💵 PRICE: 2-Day Pass (July 20+21): $89 + HST + Fees  🥗 FOOD: Available for pre-purchase at check-out or on site at venue.        BUY SUMMER FULL PASSBUY 2-DAY PASSBUY TICKETSVIEW ALL SHOWS                              ABOUT THE SHOW:  Have you met Ms. Jones? Back by popular demand, Cinnamon Jones will be returning to SOUL JAZZ in the VINEYARD. What a great way to celebrate our 10th season. This soulful Diva will have you up on your feet, waving your hands in the air, like you just don't care. Cinnamon will be coming to us from Rochester, NY and will be accompanied by some of Toronto's finest musicians. Get your tickets well in advance as this show always sells out.        ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  Behold the very essence of an unadulterated phenomenon of talent. Cinnamon Jones was designed to leave an indelible impression for all to admire. She embodies an unequaled exhibition of love and dedication for the art of music which shows through her innovative blend of genres. Her body of work reflects inspiration from gospel, Blues, Jazz, Pop, R &amp; B, and Soul. Her ability to bring together these many influences infusing them all with a Gospel core, stunning vocal prowess, and commanding stage presence, lends to a performance that is both moving and unforgettable.    Quincy Bullen is a multi-talented artist whose eclectic style and musical sensibility have won him a devoted following. With a background in classical and jazz music, Quincy has put his own twist on R&amp;B, jazz, and soul, reinvigorating modern music and contemporary jazz standards with his unique approach.    Quincy's passion for music began at an early age, and he quickly established himself as a rising star in the Canadian jazz scene. He was a founding member of the Quintessential Boys, a successful teen-jazz band that caught the attention of audiences and critics alike. Over the years, Quincy has assembled a band of up-and-coming musicians and seasoned jazz professionals to join him on his musical journey.  OPENING ACT  Tamiya Cox will be opening for this event.  Tamiya Cox  was the winner in the Ages 15-17 (Solo Vocals) category in our 2023 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Competition. CLICK HERE to see their full bio.  EMCEE  This event is Emceed by Bill King. CLICK HERE to see their full bio.        PLEASE NOTE:      Physical/digital tickets are not issued for this show. Admission is tracked through the order placed and will be added to the event’s guest list. Please retain your Order Confirmation email in case proof of purchase is require.    Tickets are non-refundable. Artists and venues are subject to change. Please visit our Health and Safety page for updates on our current guidelines.    Artists and venues subject to change.    This event will take place rain or shine.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          HOSTED BY THE HARE WINE CO.        To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASSBUY TICKETSVIEW ALL SHOWS  &nbsp;  Supported in part by:    Hospitality Sponsor  "
      }
    ],
