      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/james-bryan-in-your-own-backyard-2020-guitar-series-part-four/"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://niagarajazzfestival.com/events/james-bryan-in-your-own-backyard-2020-guitar-series-part-four"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DATE:             Monday, March 30, 2020  TIME:              7:00 pm – 9:30 pm  VENUE:          Your OWN back yard  TICKETS:       FREE but donations welcome...    This event will be  LIVE STREAMED on our FB Channel:  CLICK HERE for access.  If you plan to tune in to any of our events via live streaming, we will gladly accept donations to help us pay for the artist fees.  Either click on the Donate Now button below, for any donation amount.  Please note that we are able to issue a Charitable Tax receipt for any donation of $25 or more)    Thank you in advance.                ABOUT JAMES:    An evening of acoustic guitar magic with one of Canada’s top guitarists, James Bryan. A Latin Grammy and Juno winning performer, songwriter/producer and native of St. Catharines, James is known as a member of Canadian acts Philosopher Kings and Prozzak. James has also recorded and performed with an international roster of stars including Shawn Mendes, Nelly Furtado, and many more. But at the heart of all his music is his unmistakable guitar style. Melodic and passionate, James makes his acoustic guitar sound like an entire band, showcasing originals from his new album, Hush, and interpretations of classics from Bob Marley to Stevie Wonder.    For more information please visit www.jamesbryanmusic.com    &nbsp;    ABOUT HAMMERQUEST 2:    James will be joined by a very special opening act, youth band from Ryson's Music: Ryson's Hammerquest 2.    Hammerquest 2 has performed at the Kawanis Music Festival where they received a 95 First Class Standings. They have play at the Festival of Stars, St. Catharines Open Streets, Grape and Wine Festival, Queen Victoria Park in Niagara Falls for the Winter Festival of Lights and many other community events. The band is comprised of:    Kayleigh Doiron, 9, Guitar  Julianna Marcel, 13, Vocals and Guitar  Damian Wilson, 12, Guitar. Ukulele, Vocals  Jagger Scott, 11, Drums  James Muir, 13, Bass    &nbsp;          SCHEDULE:    6:00 pm    Doors  7:00 pm    Opening Act:  Hammerquest 2 (Youth Band)  7:20 pm    Feature Act, First Set  8:10 pm    Break  8:30 pm    Feature Act, Second Set  9:30 pm    End of Show      ABOUT THE &quot;IN YOUR OWN BACKYARD&quot; GUITAR SERIES:  The TD Niagara Jazz Festival is pleased to present this 4-part series featuring four of Canada’s finest jazz guitar artists.  The series will be presented in a 35-seat intimate setting at a private studio located in the North end of St. Catharines (close to Niagara-on-the-Lake).  For privacy reasons, the secret location is only revealed upon purchase of tickets or passes. Please note that the location is fully accessible. There will be a cash bar on-site and complimentary light fare will be served.  Doors open at 6:00 pm. All shows are from 7:00 pm to 9:30 pm and include an opening act and a refreshment break.          THE FULL SERIES INCLUDES:  PART ONE: Monday, February 10, 2020  Nathan Hiltz Trio with Pat Collins and Morgan Childs  PART TWO: Monday, February 24, 2020 Ted Quinlan Duo with Mike Downes  PART THREE: Monday, March 9, 2020 RegSchwager Duo with Duncan Hopkins  PART FOUR: Monday, March 30, 2020 James Bryan Solo  *For single tickets click on artists' names.*"
      }
    ],
