    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DATE:             Sunday, December 13, 2020  TIME:              3:30 pm – 4:00 pm EST  VENUE:          Shady Acres (This event will be Livestreamed)  PRICE:           FREE (Donations accepted)      Watch livestream on Facebook    Watch livestream on YouTube        Tracy is a national and international award winning Jewellery designer, goldsmith, and gemologist with over 27 years of experience of creating one-of-a-kind pieces. Donated by Tracy Borlase Jewellery, those who make donations of $25 or more through our fundraiser will be entered to win:      One (1) round diamond  Two (2) fine, round blue Sapphires  (Total weight: .35ct TW)  One (1) design consultation to create a piece of jewellery for the gemstones.    Total Prize Value: $700    The draw will take place on December 13th at 4pm. All donations of $25 or more from now until December 13 will be entered into the draw.                To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!  ABOUT HOME FOR THE HOLIDAYS        The TD Niagara Jazz Festival is excited to announce that this year's holiday-themed fundraising concert event will again put the &quot;fun&quot; in &quot;fundraising&quot; by presenting a joyous live-streamed celebration.    Join us on Sunday, December 6th from 4:00 PM to 5:00 PM ET for HOME for the HOLIDAYS, a FREE online virtual &quot;Sing-along&quot; featuring Jane Lewis and two-time Juno Award nominee Andrew McPherson.  Jane and Andrew will be joined by numerous special guests so be sure to tune in for a fun afternoon for the whole family!    Tenja Hagenberg  Shea D Duo  John Neudorf    Now – more than ever – it is essential to not only support the arts in general – but more specifically, we need to support the musicians and other artists who have been so financially decimated during the COVID-19 pandemic.    HOME for the HOLIDAYS will be a virtual holiday fundraiser that will support the TD Niagara Jazz Festival in their continued objective to build and sustain a community that is focused on a “shared arts experience”. The fundraiser will benefit not only the TD Niagara Jazz Festival, but also “The Anita Project” (via the United Way), which packs and distributes hygiene kits to several agencies in the Niagara region, including; Gillian’s Place, The YMCA, and Community Care.    Featuring music from the West Coast of Canada to the West Country of the UK, and tons of local Niagara talent!! Bringing the Holiday spirit right into your home, straight from Niagara!      Andrew McPherson    Jane Lewis            JAZZ at HOME Club...    In 2021, TD NJF VIP events for donors and sponsors will be hosted at Shady Acres Studio in St. Catharines. (The home of the co-creators of the festival, Juliet Dunn and Peter Shea). As we anticipating the continuation of the COVID-19 pandemic into the new year, our whole team is committed to safety and protecting our audience, artists and team to the best of our ability and in line with the most up-to-date public health mandates.                    Above:  Juliet Dunn &amp; Peter Shea at the new performance venue at Shady Acres.    Photo:  Mike Balsom for NOTL Local    Donate or sponsor today to be invited to one of these private summer VIP events. They are truly special.  :)   To donate and help support the festival:      PLEASE NOTE:  Individual VIP Invitations will go out to all donors or sponsors from the $250 + level, and the VIP event will include live music, with some of Canada's premier jazz talent,  light fare, and a complimentary beverage.    &nbsp;      "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "HOME for the HOLIDAYS Sing-Along Fundraiser Grand Prize Draw"
      }
    ],
