    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "LIVE LEARN JAZZ Series    Presented by the Niagara-on-the-Lake Public Library and the TD Niagara Jazz Festival    For the 2018 season, the TD Niagara Jazz Festival teams up once again with the NOTL Public Library and combines the LIVE LEARN JAZZ Program with a series of four concerts.    The program features Canadian artists from across Canada, and explores Canadian contributions to jazz. All sessions are curated by Canadian ethnomusicologist: Michael Morse.    Part ONE:    TAP, TAPAS and TAPS  featuring  DAVID COX (Tap) and the Attila Fias Duo    What do you get if your looking for world class jazz , paired with world class TAP footwork ,all the while enjoying some of the regions tastiest TAPAS and finest brews on TAP ? You get TAP TAPAS and TAPS of course!! Be sure and book your ticket early for this exciting and very unique experience.        David Cox: Tap  Attila Fias: Piano  Clark Johnston: Bass    Live - the experience  Learn - the history  Jazz - the music    *** This program is made possible in part by the generous support of the Town of Niagara-on-the-Lake, the Province of Ontario (Ontario Media Development Corporation, Celebrate Ontario) and the City of St. Catharines. ***    * The LIVE LEARN JAZZ Program is a satellite project of the TD Niagara Jazz Festival that was started to the lead up to the 2016 festival. It was conceived for those patrons who are interested in learning more about jazz music in a fun atmosphere, in a picturesque Niagara setting. *    Part TWO: Thursday, May 3rd - Porter and Porter at the Exchange Brewery  Part THREE: Thursday, June 7th - Vaughan in the Vines at Stratus Vineyards  Part FOUR: Thursday, July 5th -Sax in the Vineyard at the Henry of Pelham Winery    Click HERE to join the event on Facebook."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
