    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "📅 DATE: Saturday, July 22, 2023  🕑 TIME: 11:00 am – 7:00 pm   🏟️ VENUE: Simcoe Park  🗺️ ADDRESS: Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵 PRICE (Ticket): FREE*  🥗 FOOD: Various Food and drink vendors   🪑 SEATING:  Bring a lawn chair! (VIP seating for Pass Holders)  * Sign up for this FREE event and be entered for a chance to win tickets for one of the TD NJF Fall events.           SCHEDULEBUY SUMMER PASSESSIGN UPBUY WEEKEND PASS #1BUY WEEKEND PASS #2VIEW ALL SHOWS                              ABOUT THE EVENT:  This FREE event features both Jazz and World Music Artists and will take place at Simcoe Park in Niagara-on-the-Lake on Saturday, July 22nd from 11 am - 7 pm.  This event will include the following:      Two (2) music stages    Free dance lessons (Salsa and African)    Artisan Vendors    Food vendors    Wine and Beer    H2Only water tent (complimentary)    Activation area    Kids zone including painting murals, games    Splash pad    VIP seating area for pass holders    Community partners    and more!    CLICK HERE to sign up and be sure to bring your lawn chair*!    * Sign up for this FREE event and be entered for a chance to win tickets for one of the TD Niagara Jazz Festival Fall events.           ABOUT THE ARTISTS:  MUSIC in the PARK will feature an array of talented Canadian and International Jazz and World Music artists, including but not limited to:  Bobby Carcassés, Heather Bambrick, Lorraine Klaasen, Ernesto Cervini's Turboprop, Red Light Sessions, PK Hummingbird Steel Band various youth performers (sponsored by McGarr Realty Corp.) and many more!  OPENING ACT  Jonah Tredway will be opening for this event.  Jonah Tredway was the winner in the Ages 11 and Under (Solo Piano) category in our 2023 JAZZ 4 the AGES Youth Competition. CLICK HERE to see their full bio.    &nbsp;    &nbsp;          Bobby Carcassés      Heather Bambrick      Lorraine Klaasen          Ernesto Cervini's Turboprop      Red Light Sessions      PK Hummingbird Steel Orchestra          Lating Swing Orchestra      Randy Stirtzinger      Two Family Band          Jonah Tredway              &nbsp;        SCHEDULE  [table id=46 /]        PLEASE NOTE:      Artists and venues are subject to change.    This event will take place rain or shine.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com.          &nbsp;  To donate and help support the festival:    Donations to the TD Niagara Jazz Festival (Registered Charity: #80107-7033-RR0001) help us continue to bring live music to Niagara and beyond. Thank you for supporting the arts!          BUY SUMMER PASSESSIGN UPBUY WEEKEND PASSBUY 2-DAY PASSVIEW ALL SHOWS  &nbsp;  Supported in part by:      Fiesta stage sponsor    Seasoned Citizen sponsor        Youth sponsor    Water tent sponsor    "
      }
    ],
