      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/performer": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "  📅DATE: Monday, April 6th, 2026  🕑TIME: 7 pm – 9:30 pm  🏟️VENUE: The Hare Wine Co.  🗺️ADDRESS: 789 Niagara Stone Road, Niagara-on-the-Lake, ON  💵PRICE (REGULAR): $39 + HST + FEES  💵DISCOUNT (Promo Code - MAWSU-2026): -50% (19.50) + HST + FEES   (Musicians/Arts Workers/Students/Under 30)  🍕 FOOD: Snack foods available on site.   🍷DRINKS: Wine by the glass available  🚗 PARKING: Free on site     *Doors at 6 pm / Concert starts at 7 pm                 BUY TICKETS          BUY a SERIES PASS      ABOUT THE SHOW          🎶 CUBAN JAZZ NIGHT 🎶      Cuban Jazz Night with the Miguel de Armas Trio promises a vibrant and unforgettable musical experience as Cuban-born, Ottawa-based pianist and composer Miguel de Armas brings his music to Twilight Jazz &amp; Blues Series. Known for his dynamic blend of Afro-Cuban rhythms and contemporary jazz, Miguel will present an exciting program of original compositions, showcasing the rich musical language he has developed throughout his career.      Joined by the exceptional Marc Decho on bass and Ahmed Mitchel on drums, the trio will deliver an electrifying performance filled with rhythmic intensity, lyrical melodies, and inspired improvisation. Together, they create a powerful and intimate sound that captures the spirit and sophistication of modern Cuban jazz.  With limited seating at the Hare Wine Co., this special performance offers a rare opportunity to experience Cuban Jazz up close. Advance tickets are highly recommended—secure your spot and immerse yourself in a captivating night of live music.      Miguel de Armas:  Piano  Marc Decho:  Bass  Amhed Mitchel:  Drums        &nbsp;                ABOUT THE ARTISTS      Miguel de Armas is a dynamic Cuban-born pianist known for his vibrant blend of Afro-Cuban rhythms and contemporary jazz. A fixture on the jazz scene in Toronto, he brings dazzling technique, rich musicality, and infectious energy to every performance. His playing captures the spirit of Cuban jazz, weaving together rhythmic fire, lyrical melodies, and inspired improvisation.                                  BUY TICKETS          BUY a SERIES PASS                              Presented by    Juliet Amanda Dunn Entertainment                     In partnership with          Sponsored by:                          BUY TICKETS          BUY a SERIES PASS                                        PLEASE NOTE:      Tickets are non-refundable.    For more details, please email Darlene at admin@niagarajazzfestival.com                        "
      }
    ],
